Unknown: Yeah.

01:15:10.640 --> 01:15:17.240
DM: She w- never really, like, flies over here is your impression, but she has, you know, she's powerful enough everybody's afraid of her.

01:15:17.240 --> 01:15:19.620
Unknown: Everybody knows she could kill you without much of a-

01:15:20.040 --> 01:15:20.260
Unknown: Yeah

01:15:20.260 --> 01:15:23.620
DM: ... doubt, so if she says this tower is yours, nobody-

01:15:24.000 --> 01:15:24.180
Unknown: Yeah, yeah

01:15:24.180 --> 01:15:29.780
DM: ... takes it. But your sense is, like, a lot of the towers, it's like constant jostling for who gets to-

01:15:29.840 --> 01:15:30.380
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, yeah

01:15:30.380 --> 01:15:37.460
DM: ... possess something. So like he's got a pretty good place right now, but there's some, like, bigger groups that are kind of eyeing it, and so he's like, "We gotta get-

01:15:37.900 --> 01:15:38.100
Unknown: Yeah

01:15:38.100 --> 01:15:38.920
DM: ... backup," right?

01:15:38.980 --> 01:15:39.000
Unknown: Yeah.

01:15:39.000 --> 01:15:42.920
DM: "We gotta get Ra'ghemdros to say this is ours and then we'll be nice and..."

01:15:42.920 --> 01:15:43.440
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, yeah. Interesting.

01:15:44.820 --> 01:15:45.500
Unknown: Interesting.

01:15:45.500 --> 01:15:54.640
DM: But the other thing you said, the other bits of information you learned is, like, there are literally no coins, gems, jewelry anywhere on the island.

01:15:54.640 --> 01:15:57.900
DM: Like, they've been scouring this island for generations.

01:15:58.160 --> 01:15:58.420
Unknown: Yeah.

01:15:58.420 --> 01:16:01.280
DM: And there is not... Like, that's why people started going to the mainland.

01:16:01.520 --> 01:16:01.880
Unknown: Ah.

01:16:01.880 --> 01:16:04.020
Unknown: 'Cause there's like literally nothing left to find.

01:16:04.360 --> 01:16:06.380
Wellby: Ask him what's in the towers at the center of it.

01:16:07.220 --> 01:16:08.340
Unknown: Yeah, what's in the center of this place?

01:16:09.260 --> 01:16:10.240
DM: Oh, in the forest?

01:16:11.240 --> 01:16:14.120
DM: That's, that's kind of a strange vibe.

01:16:14.120 --> 01:16:15.640
DM: There's like a monastery there.

01:16:17.340 --> 01:16:18.720
Unknown: A monastery? Huh.

01:16:18.760 --> 01:16:18.840
Unknown: A monastery.

01:16:18.840 --> 01:16:21.400
DM: I mean, nothing left to find, but...

01:16:22.120 --> 01:16:22.980
Unknown: A human monastery?

01:16:23.060 --> 01:16:24.280
DM: Yeah, I think it's human.

01:16:24.580 --> 01:16:25.420
Unknown: Huh.

01:16:25.440 --> 01:16:31.800
DM: It's got like eight buildings with like stat- with like statues that look like the statues.

01:16:32.000 --> 01:16:33.980
Delwath: Is this in the forest or on the top of a mountain?

01:16:34.340 --> 01:16:37.120
DM: On the top. The forest we don't really go into.

01:16:37.760 --> 01:16:38.160
Unknown: Why not?

01:16:40.240 --> 01:16:40.840
DM: Um,

01:16:41.960 --> 01:16:45.920
DM: sometimes if you're flying around, like, the elvish voices tell you to leave,

01:16:47.000 --> 01:16:48.480
DM: and we don't mess with them.

01:16:49.200 --> 01:16:49.840
Unknown: Elvish voices.

01:16:49.880 --> 01:16:50.660
Unknown: Are they scary?

01:16:52.600 --> 01:16:55.980
DM: I mean, yeah, when a tree says, "This is my garden.

01:16:55.980 --> 01:16:58.060
DM: Leave," I wouldn't mess with them.

01:16:58.400 --> 01:16:58.600
Unknown: True.

01:16:58.620 --> 01:17:00.160
Unknown: A tree, a talking tree.

01:17:00.180 --> 01:17:00.300
Unknown: Hmm.

01:17:01.380 --> 01:17:03.100
Kenzo: And is Ra'ghemdros in the center of the island?

01:17:03.960 --> 01:17:04.280
DM: No, we know-

01:17:04.320 --> 01:17:04.800
Unknown: Or on the west

01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:06.000
DM: ... that the tower's just to the south.

01:17:06.080 --> 01:17:06.420
Unknown: Oh, we're on the south.

01:17:06.420 --> 01:17:08.300
DM: That's her, that's where she lives, right over there.

01:17:08.620 --> 01:17:08.960
Unknown: Yeah.

01:17:08.980 --> 01:17:14.280
Wellby: Is anyone in the tower, like in the monastery at the center, or is it totally empty?

01:17:14.360 --> 01:17:15.860
Unknown: No, it's totally empty.

01:17:15.860 --> 01:17:19.820
Seeker: Maybe Ra'ghemdros is the entity that is both guardian and, and trapped.

01:17:19.900 --> 01:17:20.040
DM: Yeah, I think so.

01:17:20.040 --> 01:17:22.880
Seeker: You could just free her instead of killing her.

01:17:25.180 --> 01:17:25.480
Unknown: I mean,

01:17:26.480 --> 01:17:27.180
Unknown: free her to go

01:17:28.220 --> 01:17:30.460
Delwath: fly around rampaging Talgar?

01:17:30.600 --> 01:17:30.760
Unknown: I mean-

01:17:30.760 --> 01:17:32.600
Seeker: Well, who knows what her motivation is, really

01:17:32.600 --> 01:17:33.820
Unknown: ... what's, what's going on on the west side?

01:17:33.820 --> 01:17:35.480
Delwath: Kill people and take their stuff?

01:17:35.580 --> 01:17:36.420
DM: Oh, that's the one place we don't go.

01:17:36.420 --> 01:17:37.560
Unknown: That could just be a hobby. Who knows?

01:17:37.560 --> 01:17:38.640
Unknown: Why does she, why don't you go there?

01:17:38.640 --> 01:17:42.960
Wellby: [laughs] There's, there's like 11 one places that we don't go.

01:17:42.960 --> 01:17:44.280
Unknown: [laughs]

01:17:44.280 --> 01:17:44.379
DM: [laughs]

01:17:44.460 --> 01:17:46.920
Kenzo: Feels like there's a lot of hostile stuff going on on this ta- this island.

01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:47.920
DM: Um,

01:17:49.200 --> 01:17:51.740
DM: it's like some ancient war.

01:17:51.740 --> 01:17:58.080
DM: Uh, I don't really know the details, but Ra'ghemdros told us not to bother with it.

01:18:00.080 --> 01:18:01.600
Unknown: So none of you have snuck over there?

01:18:04.140 --> 01:18:06.880
DM: I haven't.

01:18:06.880 --> 01:18:08.280
DM: I don't know. Maybe somebody has.

01:18:10.300 --> 01:18:12.280
Kenzo: But you must have like, you know, searched for coin there.

01:18:15.360 --> 01:18:15.720
DM: Um,

01:18:18.740 --> 01:18:20.140
DM: no.

01:18:20.140 --> 01:18:20.580
DM: So

01:18:23.200 --> 01:18:23.780
DM: we're told

01:18:25.360 --> 01:18:27.300
DM: that that's the one place where

01:18:28.620 --> 01:18:29.300
DM: if we go,

01:18:30.680 --> 01:18:32.880
DM: we might provoke real danger.

01:18:33.820 --> 01:18:36.000
Kenzo: What does that mean, provoke real danger?

01:18:36.020 --> 01:18:39.140
DM: I don't know. I think it's something Ra'ghemdros doesn't wanna deal with.

01:18:40.940 --> 01:18:41.460
Unknown: Hmm.

01:18:43.280 --> 01:18:43.900
Unknown: Ancient danger?

01:18:45.380 --> 01:18:47.420
DM: I mean, everything's ancient here, right?

01:18:47.420 --> 01:18:51.380
DM: Nothing's changed on the island for generations and generations and generations.

01:18:51.380 --> 01:18:52.220
Unknown: Do you know who made the island?

01:18:54.500 --> 01:18:55.480
DM: I think we did.

01:18:56.420 --> 01:18:56.800
Unknown: Really?

01:18:57.860 --> 01:18:59.440
Kenzo: You made the island? You guys made this island?

01:18:59.500 --> 01:19:00.400
DM: Our ancestors.

01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:01.600
Unknown: Are you magic?

01:19:02.740 --> 01:19:03.660
DM: I mean, I can fly.

01:19:04.160 --> 01:19:05.760
Kenzo: Yeah, you can fly, but can you like cast spells?

01:19:05.760 --> 01:19:08.200
Kenzo: Can you do anything cool? [laughs]

01:19:08.260 --> 01:19:08.980
Unknown: Oh, damn.

01:19:08.980 --> 01:19:09.480
DM: Really?

01:19:09.780 --> 01:19:10.260
Unknown: Yeah.

01:19:10.280 --> 01:19:11.480
DM: That's what you want to know?

01:19:11.560 --> 01:19:12.600
Unknown: I'm curious.

01:19:12.600 --> 01:19:13.680
DM: I mean, I can fight.

01:19:14.140 --> 01:19:14.440
Unknown: Like how?

01:19:14.460 --> 01:19:14.980
DM: A little bit.

01:19:16.100 --> 01:19:16.780
DM: Like, you know...

01:19:18.960 --> 01:19:19.120
DM: [whooshing]

01:19:19.120 --> 01:19:20.800
Kenzo: [laughs] Come on. What else can you do?

01:19:22.180 --> 01:19:22.840
Unknown: You cast any spells?

01:19:22.960 --> 01:19:24.520
Unknown: I beat you at dice.

01:19:24.520 --> 01:19:25.940
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'll give you that.

01:19:25.960 --> 01:19:27.280
Unknown: You beat me at dice. That's fine.

01:19:27.280 --> 01:19:29.960
Kenzo: But come on, me and you in a fight, let's be real.

01:19:35.410 --> 01:19:38.150
Kenzo: I'm not saying that you're not, you know, you don't have any things going for you.

01:19:38.150 --> 01:19:39.610
Kenzo: I mean, it's pretty fucking cool that you can fly.

01:19:39.610 --> 01:19:41.370
Kenzo: I need a whistle to fly. You can just do it yourself.

01:19:41.430 --> 01:19:44.050
Seeker: That's pretty sweet. We definitely need to, like, indenture a group of these guys to do stuff.

01:19:44.110 --> 01:19:46.950
DM: I mean, yeah, some people can cast spells.

01:19:46.990 --> 01:19:47.850
Kenzo: Well, if we kill- Oh, really?

01:19:48.310 --> 01:19:48.670
DM: Huh

01:19:48.670 --> 01:19:50.930
Seeker: ... some of your friends can cast spells. If we kill the dragon, they'll be free all of a sudden.

01:19:51.010 --> 01:19:51.190
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:19:52.610 --> 01:19:54.070
Kenzo: We'll just adopt them. Yeah.

01:19:54.250 --> 01:19:54.590
Kenzo: That would work.

01:19:54.630 --> 01:19:54.950
DM: Yeah.

01:19:55.730 --> 01:19:56.350
Kenzo: We, we-

01:19:56.430 --> 01:19:57.150
DM: A few people.

01:19:57.970 --> 01:19:59.730
Seeker: We have little corners for 100 tiny dragons under here

01:19:59.730 --> 01:20:01.590
DM: ... I mean, not, like, humans. Like, some humans can cast spells, right?

01:20:01.990 --> 01:20:08.250
DM: I've heard stories anyway. I mean, if you look in the, some of the buildings, there's clearly, like, paintings of people casting spells.

01:20:09.590 --> 01:20:09.750
Kenzo: Hmm.

01:20:11.530 --> 01:20:13.070
Wellby: What would they do if Ra'ghemdros left?

01:20:13.150 --> 01:20:14.170
Kenzo: I was just gonna say.

01:20:15.030 --> 01:20:17.530
Kenzo: So, like, what if, what if Ra'ghemdros wasn't here?

01:20:18.850 --> 01:20:27.710
DM: How is that possible? [dice rolling] I, I've never even considered the possibility.

01:20:28.190 --> 01:20:28.990
Kenzo: Yeah, but what if she left?

01:20:30.410 --> 01:20:33.690
DM: I mean, that's like saying what if there was no sun.

01:20:34.750 --> 01:20:35.710
Kenzo: Yeah, well, I'm asking.

01:20:36.550 --> 01:20:37.710
DM: I don't know. It would be different.

01:20:38.570 --> 01:20:39.590
Kenzo: But would you, would things be better?

01:20:42.870 --> 01:20:43.710
DM: I mean,

01:20:44.990 --> 01:20:47.330
DM: I can't say I'm, like, fond of her.

01:20:47.330 --> 01:20:49.070
Kenzo: That's what I'm saying. It feels like she, I mean,

01:20:49.990 --> 01:20:53.550
Kenzo: s- j... I mean, again, I'm, I'm, I'm new here, but just feels like

01:20:54.470 --> 01:20:56.170
Kenzo: you kinda gotta run everything by her.

01:20:56.170 --> 01:20:57.730
Kenzo: She controls who gets what.

01:20:57.730 --> 01:21:03.270
Kenzo: You gotta get, you know, it's like, feels like somebody like you in particular, y- you, you know, you're, you're...

01:21:10.530 --> 01:21:12.070
DM: I, I would not mourn at her funeral.

01:21:12.750 --> 01:21:15.010
Kenzo: That's the feeling I get. It's the feeling I get.

01:21:15.450 --> 01:21:16.370
DM: There are some who would.

01:21:16.870 --> 01:21:17.110
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:21:18.190 --> 01:21:19.310
Kenzo: Hmm. Fair.

01:21:20.510 --> 01:21:20.930
Kenzo: It's fair.

01:21:21.930 --> 01:21:22.050
DM: So-

01:21:22.090 --> 01:21:22.630
Kenzo: Let's get to the tower

01:21:22.630 --> 01:21:25.350
DM: ... you get to the tower. Um, there's definitely more...

01:21:25.350 --> 01:21:31.190
DM: So you can see as you approach, like he flies up and he, like, you know, talks to a few people and, and introdu...

01:21:31.190 --> 01:21:36.550
DM: you know, g- gives them a little bit of a story and like, you know, don't, this is hush-hush.

01:21:36.550 --> 01:21:39.350
DM: Like, you can tell he's trying to pr- preserve his, like-

01:21:39.450 --> 01:21:39.910
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah

01:21:39.910 --> 01:21:40.930
DM: ... his edge here.

01:21:41.010 --> 01:21:41.310
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:21:41.310 --> 01:21:41.490
DM: Um,

01:21:42.970 --> 01:21:45.230
DM: this is a, this is, this is much nicer.

01:21:45.230 --> 01:21:51.830
DM: So the, the tower here is, uh, this looks like a sort of traditional wizard's tower, right?

01:21:51.830 --> 01:21:52.410
DM: Like it's-

01:21:52.430 --> 01:21:52.990
Kenzo: Hmm

01:21:52.990 --> 01:21:55.490
DM: ... uh, you know, 100 feet tall.

01:21:55.490 --> 01:21:55.890
Kenzo: Wow.

01:21:55.890 --> 01:21:56.150
DM: Um,

01:21:57.270 --> 01:22:07.290
DM: c- basically completely int- intact except for, um, it looks like there once might have been a spire or something on the top [dice rolling] that's sort of cracked

01:22:07.290 --> 01:22:16.330
DM: and has been crudely re-roofed, um, with just sort of s- like jumbles of stone and stuff, so there is a, is a roof.

01:22:16.330 --> 01:22:16.490
DM: Um,

01:22:17.670 --> 01:22:20.410
DM: the, the grounds have clearly been like recently,

01:22:21.790 --> 01:22:21.930
DM: uh,

01:22:24.510 --> 01:22:28.770
DM: t- sort of tended. Like, there's a few, there's, um, what look like, uh,

01:22:30.290 --> 01:22:32.310
DM: kind of, they're not really

01:22:33.550 --> 01:22:44.210
DM: houses, but there's like almost like lean tos, like little places where people could shelter from bad weather that have been built with like just stone that's been carried, big slabs of stone that have been carried from elsewhere,

01:22:44.210 --> 01:22:46.150
DM: just kind of dropped and arranged.

01:22:46.150 --> 01:22:48.390
DM: So like it almost looks like there's a tiny little, um,

01:22:49.990 --> 01:22:55.490
DM: uh, small village around the base of this tower and the, um, like there's been...

01:22:55.490 --> 01:23:05.790
DM: There's no trees here. This was once, there's like a, there was once like a long, um, reflecting pool that went from the base of the tower that's sort of lined with marble, which is,

01:23:05.790 --> 01:23:12.850
DM: still has water in it and there's, like you can see a couple of, of, um, dragonets like diving and, and bathing in it.

01:23:12.850 --> 01:23:14.870
DM: This is like much nicer than the other tower.

01:23:15.670 --> 01:23:26.090
DM: And, um, there's probably 30 dragonets around here, um, a bigger group, and Megren flies down after,

01:23:26.090 --> 01:23:27.790
DM: um, Ghesh introduces you.

01:23:29.550 --> 01:23:33.330
DM: She's wearing, um, a, like a chain around her neck-

01:23:33.390 --> 01:23:33.650
Kenzo: Hmm

01:23:33.650 --> 01:23:43.750
DM: ... that's no- nothing like gold or metal or shiny, but it's like a, it's like a rope chain that then has this like very nice

01:23:43.750 --> 01:23:48.370
DM: sort of polished wood, um, sort of amulet, um,

01:23:49.290 --> 01:23:57.370
DM: that like clearly is like some, you know, some reward that was not shiny enough to be importantly kept in the hoard-

01:23:57.390 --> 01:23:57.450
Kenzo: Hmm

01:23:57.450 --> 01:23:58.750
DM: ... but was gifted to her.

01:23:58.770 --> 01:24:00.090
DM: It looks old. It looks like,

01:24:01.150 --> 01:24:03.930
DM: um, actually, it looks vaguely Elvish to your eyes.

01:24:03.950 --> 01:24:04.050
Kenzo: Hmm.

01:24:06.130 --> 01:24:13.390
DM: Um, and she's sort of a, a slightly bigger than Gresh, slightly greener than Gresh, more of like an olive color.

01:24:13.430 --> 01:24:13.690
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:24:13.770 --> 01:24:15.470
DM: Um, and she flies down and, um,

01:24:16.810 --> 01:24:20.990
DM: kind of gives you a little bow and, "Welcome to my humble abode."

01:24:21.630 --> 01:24:24.210
Kenzo: Kenzo also bows and, and looks up.

01:24:24.210 --> 01:24:25.470
Kenzo: This is more than humble. This is

01:24:26.530 --> 01:24:27.310
Kenzo: very, very beautiful. Very nice.

01:24:27.350 --> 01:24:32.650
DM: Well, we have been working over the past few weeks, uh, since...

01:24:34.090 --> 01:24:35.870
DM: Well, now it is mine, in fact.

01:24:37.570 --> 01:24:39.830
Kenzo: You are quite fortunate to live in such a place.

01:24:39.830 --> 01:24:40.410
Kenzo: It's beautiful.

01:24:41.610 --> 01:24:43.530
DM: I think it has potential.

01:24:44.370 --> 01:24:45.130
Kenzo: I would say so.

01:24:47.310 --> 01:24:52.270
Kenzo: So, uh, uh, Gresh here was sharing that you, uh, recently went to the mainland.

01:24:52.270 --> 01:24:52.910
Kenzo: That's where I'm from.

01:24:54.150 --> 01:24:54.710
DM: I heard.

01:24:55.190 --> 01:24:55.230
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:24:55.250 --> 01:24:56.390
DM: That was told to me.

01:24:56.490 --> 01:24:56.870
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:24:56.870 --> 01:25:01.130
DM: I'm quite interested, although not so much for myself.

01:25:01.130 --> 01:25:07.270
DM: Some of my more ambitious followers are perhaps interested in their own towers.

01:25:07.550 --> 01:25:08.210
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:25:08.210 --> 01:25:14.050
DM: I don't think I'll brave the storms anymore, but others might like to know

01:25:15.130 --> 01:25:18.210
DM: where else to look. I heard you found some

01:25:19.110 --> 01:25:23.710
DM: golden crown in some ruins in the jungle that we were not aware of.

01:25:23.810 --> 01:25:29.350
Kenzo: I did find something. I did find something there, and there are definitely other places to look.

01:25:30.950 --> 01:25:33.630
DM: I'm very interested.

01:25:33.630 --> 01:25:36.070
Delwath: Tell her you want to know the s- You're collecting stories, right?

01:25:36.330 --> 01:25:36.370
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:25:36.370 --> 01:25:38.110
Unknown: Tell her you're, like, collecting the story-

01:25:38.150 --> 01:25:38.210
Kenzo: So-

01:25:38.210 --> 01:25:39.470
DM: ... of her amazing heroism.

01:25:39.670 --> 01:25:44.750
Kenzo: Yeah, so, so when you, when you came to, uh, um, to the, uh, uh, to the mainland-

01:25:44.790 --> 01:25:46.130
DM: You're... Are you carrying your staff?

01:25:46.910 --> 01:25:51.290
Kenzo: So, yes. So I am carrying my staff, but I've been, um...

01:25:51.290 --> 01:25:55.690
Kenzo: Like, I can carry it in a way that's, like, like, uh, I'm-

01:25:56.670 --> 01:25:58.490
Delwath: But there's pieces of jade, I think, on the top.

01:25:58.490 --> 01:25:58.670
DM: Is that correct?

01:25:58.670 --> 01:26:00.430
Kenzo: There is on the top, yeah. I mean, that, that's the-

01:26:00.470 --> 01:26:01.350
DM: There's four pieces of jade on the top.

01:26:01.370 --> 01:26:03.610
Kenzo: Yeah. The, the top is the most, uh, the most...

01:26:03.610 --> 01:26:05.150
Kenzo: But, but I, I've been keeping that-

01:26:05.490 --> 01:26:05.650
DM: Okay

01:26:05.650 --> 01:26:07.050
Kenzo: ... the, the top, like, not...

01:26:07.070 --> 01:26:07.590
Kenzo: You know?

01:26:07.630 --> 01:26:09.630
DM: You can probably use Dreamcraft to cause a flower to grow on the staff.

01:26:09.710 --> 01:26:10.310
Wellby: Oh, you could.

01:26:10.550 --> 01:26:10.990
Kenzo: Oh, perfect.

01:26:11.010 --> 01:26:11.530
DM: That's smart.

01:26:11.530 --> 01:26:12.810
Kenzo: That's perfect. I'll, I'll do that instead.

01:26:12.870 --> 01:26:12.930
DM: Okay.

01:26:12.930 --> 01:26:14.030
Kenzo: Yeah, so it's just, it's just a more-

01:26:14.050 --> 01:26:15.630
Unknown: So it looks like it's, like, the flowers are-

01:26:15.730 --> 01:26:16.950
Kenzo: It's all, it's all, uh, it's all wooden.

01:26:16.950 --> 01:26:17.890
Kenzo: It's all... looks like just-

01:26:17.910 --> 01:26:18.010
DM: Yeah

01:26:18.010 --> 01:26:19.390
Kenzo: ... a full, totally wooden staff.

01:26:19.950 --> 01:26:20.030
DM: Yeah, yeah.

01:26:20.050 --> 01:26:20.270
Kenzo: Um,

01:26:21.510 --> 01:26:22.850
Kenzo: but, uh, but yeah.

01:26:22.870 --> 01:26:27.910
Kenzo: But, uh, but Gresh says you, uh, you found some interesting things in the, uh, uh, your, your last visit.

01:26:27.970 --> 01:26:29.850
DM: Yeah. It was quite an interesting...

01:26:29.850 --> 01:26:31.750
DM: So I've been a few times.

01:26:31.810 --> 01:26:32.030
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:26:33.330 --> 01:26:36.110
DM: Um, it's hard to get too far inland, 'cause there's...

01:26:36.110 --> 01:26:42.330
DM: You know, the monkeys are annoying, and you've got to fly very high, and then all the interesting places to look have, like,

01:26:43.990 --> 01:26:46.130
DM: bothersome people living in them.

01:26:46.650 --> 01:26:46.950
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:26:47.090 --> 01:26:49.910
DM: But I found this cave that seemed empty.

01:26:49.910 --> 01:26:50.930
Kenzo: Hmm.

01:26:50.930 --> 01:26:54.070
DM: I flew around a little bit, and like, mostly it was boring stuff.

01:26:54.070 --> 01:26:57.390
DM: It was, like, dried mango or garbage like that.

01:26:57.390 --> 01:26:58.810
DM: Nobody would care about that here.

01:26:59.410 --> 01:27:02.010
DM: Um, food's never really a problem, right?

01:27:02.010 --> 01:27:02.190
DM: Um,

01:27:04.470 --> 01:27:05.670
DM: what do they eat?

01:27:05.670 --> 01:27:06.610
Kenzo: Probably fish.

01:27:06.650 --> 01:27:07.730
DM: Hmm. Or do they just-

01:27:07.730 --> 01:27:08.170
Wellby: Or the circles

01:27:08.170 --> 01:27:09.730
DM: ... sit down on one of the arcane circles?

01:27:09.770 --> 01:27:13.250
Unknown: Oh, right. Of course. [laughs]

01:27:13.370 --> 01:27:15.090
DM: Oh. Uh, but there was this

01:27:16.470 --> 01:27:20.550
DM: big green gem that was just sitting there.

01:27:20.550 --> 01:27:23.430
DM: Like, whoever found it didn't even know what they had found.

01:27:23.910 --> 01:27:27.270
DM: Why would you just leave that sitting out and not protect it or anything?

01:27:27.910 --> 01:27:29.310
DM: I mean, she holds up her hand.

01:27:29.310 --> 01:27:32.990
DM: It was, like, the size of my claw, just like the size of all the other dragons.

01:27:33.030 --> 01:27:33.190
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:27:34.810 --> 01:27:34.830
DM: Yeah.

01:27:34.850 --> 01:27:38.910
Kenzo: But by the way, um, the, the wood, you know, that's just how it always looks.

01:27:38.910 --> 01:27:40.730
Kenzo: The staff normally does not look like it's got, like-

01:27:40.770 --> 01:27:40.890
DM: Yeah, yeah

01:27:40.890 --> 01:27:41.930
Kenzo: ... four giant huge pieces of j-

01:27:42.050 --> 01:27:42.409
DM: So it's... Right

01:27:42.409 --> 01:27:44.530
Kenzo: ... it, it's, it's got, you know, in its everyday use, it is-

01:27:44.530 --> 01:27:48.410
DM: Right. Well, there's nothing about Dreamcraft that says when you cause something to bloom, the bloom dies.

01:27:48.550 --> 01:27:49.150
Kenzo: Right. Right.

01:27:49.170 --> 01:27:51.290
DM: So you just, like, make... This is, like, what the...

01:27:51.670 --> 01:27:59.430
DM: You know, remember when you were on the ship sailing to Chardin and the halfling druid was, like, touched your staff and made, like, something bloom from it?

01:27:59.750 --> 01:27:59.830
Kenzo: Cool.

01:27:59.870 --> 01:28:03.410
DM: Like, Kenzo wants to do this, so Kenzo learned how to do that, so now you can, like, summon forth.

01:28:03.410 --> 01:28:04.270
Kenzo: That's great.

01:28:04.270 --> 01:28:04.550
DM: Um-

01:28:04.550 --> 01:28:05.530
Kenzo: But that way it's just not-

01:28:05.670 --> 01:28:05.870
DM: Yeah, yeah

01:28:05.870 --> 01:28:07.430
Unknown: ... it's not so conspicuous. Yeah.

01:28:07.550 --> 01:28:07.770
DM: Uh,

01:28:08.590 --> 01:28:08.710
DM: so

01:28:09.590 --> 01:28:10.250
DM: I grabbed it.

01:28:11.230 --> 01:28:14.870
DM: Who wouldn't, right? I'm, I know, I know what side of the...

01:28:16.210 --> 01:28:19.090
DM: what side of... Well, she, uh, what's...

01:28:19.090 --> 01:28:22.990
DM: Whatever the dragonet metaphor for, like, you know, which is the right side up.

01:28:22.990 --> 01:28:23.850
DM: Like, what side of the

01:28:24.850 --> 01:28:28.890
DM: bread is buttered or whatever the metaphor is, but not bread and butter, 'cause they would kill each other.

01:28:28.890 --> 01:28:29.830
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:28:29.830 --> 01:28:31.610
DM: You know, I, I know who's in charge, right?

01:28:31.610 --> 01:28:34.970
DM: But I got a pretty good trade for it.

01:28:34.970 --> 01:28:40.190
DM: I don't think Regendros has found new gemstones in a while.

01:28:40.250 --> 01:28:40.730
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:28:43.290 --> 01:28:50.070
Kenzo: Um, in this area when we were in the jungle, uh, just like, uh, so 'cause again, I think that last time I was, I was, like, checked out.

01:28:50.550 --> 01:28:53.610
Kenzo: Are there... Were there other, like, kind of interesting...

01:28:53.610 --> 01:28:54.630
Kenzo: Did we get anything there?

01:28:54.670 --> 01:28:55.290
Wellby: No.

01:28:55.350 --> 01:28:56.590
DM: You didn't really explore.

01:28:56.750 --> 01:28:57.610
Kenzo: We didn't explore. Okay.

01:28:57.610 --> 01:28:59.950
DM: You did hear that there were other...

01:28:59.970 --> 01:29:05.170
DM: Like, further to the west, there was, like, other territory from the Awaken jungle people that

01:29:06.250 --> 01:29:07.490
DM: might have things.

01:29:07.690 --> 01:29:08.410
Kenzo: Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

01:29:08.430 --> 01:29:11.430
DM: But you were pretty focused on just tracking the jade.

01:29:11.570 --> 01:29:11.650
Kenzo: Right, right, right.

01:29:11.650 --> 01:29:12.770
DM: You explored the caves, but-

01:29:12.810 --> 01:29:13.390
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah

01:29:13.390 --> 01:29:15.390
DM: ... she obviously had been to those caves.

01:29:15.650 --> 01:29:15.750
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:29:15.750 --> 01:29:15.770
DM: Yeah.

01:29:15.790 --> 01:29:22.670
Delwath: I mean, I assume, by the way, the jade, if Kenzo senses the direction, it's pointing to The Scar.

01:29:22.730 --> 01:29:23.130
DM: Oh, yeah.

01:29:23.170 --> 01:29:23.650
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah.

01:29:23.670 --> 01:29:23.970
DM: Yeah.

01:29:23.990 --> 01:29:26.110
Kenzo: I mean, this is pretty... I mean, now I think it's pretty much just gonna-

01:29:26.170 --> 01:29:26.270
DM: Yeah

01:29:26.270 --> 01:29:27.070
Kenzo: ... point to The Scar anyway.

01:29:27.090 --> 01:29:27.090
DM: Okay.

01:29:27.090 --> 01:29:27.130
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:29:27.130 --> 01:29:32.450
Delwath: So probably we should regroup, maybe try and get out of there pretty soon.

01:29:32.490 --> 01:29:34.990
Wellby: Well, I, I wonder if there's anything else... Like, when,

01:29:36.290 --> 01:29:39.270
Wellby: when this person took the jade, they went to Regendros-

01:29:39.350 --> 01:29:39.410
Kenzo: Yeah

01:29:39.410 --> 01:29:40.290
Wellby: ... to steal it. Like, what-

01:29:40.770 --> 01:29:40.850
Kenzo: Yeah

01:29:40.850 --> 01:29:42.490
Wellby: ... what was that like? How did they get there?

01:29:42.550 --> 01:29:43.590
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah. Wait, what is-

01:29:43.650 --> 01:29:46.270
Wellby: Like, pri- prying... Like, what's the approach?

01:29:46.270 --> 01:29:50.090
Wellby: What's the lair like? Can we sneak in and kill her in her sleep?

01:29:50.090 --> 01:29:51.150
Kenzo: [laughs] Yeah.

01:29:51.150 --> 01:29:51.530
DM: Yeah, yeah.

01:29:51.530 --> 01:29:52.630
Wellby: But without making it sound like an-

01:29:52.850 --> 01:29:53.410
DM: Yeah.

01:29:53.490 --> 01:29:53.670
Kenzo: So, so-

01:29:53.690 --> 01:29:55.870
Seeker: You could, you could appeal to the vanity part.

01:29:55.910 --> 01:29:56.090
Kenzo: Right.

01:29:56.110 --> 01:29:57.470
DM: Like, oh, this tower's pretty cool.

01:29:57.510 --> 01:29:57.530
Kenzo: Yeah.

01:29:57.550 --> 01:29:58.630
DM: But what does Regendros have?

01:29:58.630 --> 01:29:58.950
Wellby: Yeah, exactly.

01:29:58.950 --> 01:30:00.810
Seeker: Like, it's like, must be, must be a little nicer, right?

01:30:00.850 --> 01:30:05.290
Kenzo: Yeah. So Regendros must have been pretty happy about this, that, uh, that, that jewel, huh?

01:30:05.790 --> 01:30:07.090
DM: Oh, yeah. For sure.

01:30:07.090 --> 01:30:07.390
DM: I mean,

01:30:08.690 --> 01:30:10.370
DM: she, like, waves her wings around.

01:30:11.250 --> 01:30:14.410
Kenzo: I mean, this is pretty nice here, but Regendros' place,

01:30:15.710 --> 01:30:17.050
Kenzo: it's gotta be a little bit nicer, right?

01:30:17.470 --> 01:30:19.070
DM: Oh, no, it's way worse.

01:30:19.070 --> 01:30:19.710
Kenzo: It's way worse?

01:30:20.250 --> 01:30:22.630
DM: I mean, she lives, like, underneath a...

01:30:25.150 --> 01:30:25.590
DM: What is it?

01:30:27.450 --> 01:30:28.930
DM: A... She, she points to the pool.

01:30:28.930 --> 01:30:31.870
DM: It's like that, but bigger. But you have to, like, swim.

01:30:31.890 --> 01:30:32.850
DM: You gotta, like, get her

01:30:34.390 --> 01:30:40.930
DM: guards to show you. You swim down, and then it's, like, this nasty, swampy, acidic mess of a cave.

01:30:41.570 --> 01:30:42.390
DM: Like, ugh.

01:30:43.010 --> 01:30:43.130
Kenzo: Wow, she-

01:30:43.270 --> 01:30:44.350
DM: This is way prettier.

01:30:44.350 --> 01:30:45.410
Kenzo: Why would she stay down there?

01:30:45.450 --> 01:30:46.450
Wellby: Hmm.

01:30:46.470 --> 01:30:49.270
DM: Well.

01:30:49.270 --> 01:30:52.350
Kenzo: You s- But she's got... You said that, uh, you can't just fly there yourself.

01:30:53.770 --> 01:30:55.050
Kenzo: You said there are people that have to let you in.

01:30:57.570 --> 01:30:59.470
DM: Well, I don't know how you would get...

01:31:00.970 --> 01:31:02.350
DM: I don't know. Maybe you could.

01:31:03.070 --> 01:31:05.510
DM: I wouldn't wanna go into her lair unannounced.

01:31:05.510 --> 01:31:06.930
DM: [coughs]

01:31:06.970 --> 01:31:08.070
Kenzo: When, when does she come out?

01:31:08.070 --> 01:31:08.730
Wellby: Yeah, why not?

01:31:10.990 --> 01:31:12.410
DM: 'Cause she'd kill me.

01:31:12.410 --> 01:31:13.390
DM: What, are you crazy?

01:31:13.870 --> 01:31:18.430
Kenzo: You said, you s- But there are a bunch of, uh, people that need to let, that need, would need to let you in, that need to let you in?

01:31:18.470 --> 01:31:21.950
DM: So when I went there, I did the thing that any sensible person would do.

01:31:21.950 --> 01:31:28.950
DM: I talked to her guards that were perched on the columns around this, like, baths or something, and they were like,

01:31:30.170 --> 01:31:31.890
Unknown: "Br, br, br, I'll talk to her.

01:31:32.290 --> 01:31:33.670
DM: Yeah, okay. You can come."

01:31:33.670 --> 01:31:33.790
Wellby: [laughs]

01:31:33.790 --> 01:31:34.430
DM: "That's good."

01:31:35.270 --> 01:31:37.650
DM: And then they, like, said, "Okay, follow me."

01:31:37.650 --> 01:31:43.360
DM: And then we dove down beneath the surface of this water, and I have to hold my breath, and then suddenly we were in a- ...

01:31:43.360 --> 01:31:52.540
DM: cavern dripping acid and we flew over an acid lake and passed some like nasty, dark, shadowy tendrils of gooey evil.

01:31:53.740 --> 01:31:54.300
DM: And then

01:31:56.460 --> 01:32:03.240
DM: her lair is like this horrific mass of g- acidic geysers that she, like, drinks from for no reason.

01:32:03.260 --> 01:32:04.100
Kenzo: We need to get her out of there.

01:32:04.320 --> 01:32:04.520
Unknown: We do.

01:32:04.520 --> 01:32:05.700
Kenzo: We need to fight her not in there.

01:32:05.780 --> 01:32:07.700
Delwath: There's... She probably can't leave.

01:32:07.700 --> 01:32:07.840
Kenzo: We gotta get her out.

01:32:07.840 --> 01:32:08.920
Unknown: That's the prison guard.

01:32:08.920 --> 01:32:11.380
DM: [gasps]

01:32:11.480 --> 01:32:11.720
Kenzo: Oh.

01:32:13.200 --> 01:32:14.800
Seeker: Oh. Uh, or, well, just a- let's find out.

01:32:15.100 --> 01:32:19.240
DM: When does she come out? But when I gave it to her, she did like seem pretty happy.

01:32:20.160 --> 01:32:21.160
Unknown: So she never comes out of there?

01:32:21.160 --> 01:32:27.300
DM: [sucks teeth] I don't know.

01:32:27.980 --> 01:32:30.160
Kenzo: Has anybody ever seen her not in there?

01:32:32.360 --> 01:32:33.460
DM: Yeah, once.

01:32:34.420 --> 01:32:35.500
DM: Well, I didn't see it.

01:32:36.560 --> 01:32:38.080
DM: Friend of a friend told me a story.

01:32:38.620 --> 01:32:39.840
Kenzo: What's the story? How'd she get out of there?

01:32:42.520 --> 01:32:44.960
DM: Well [laughs] this is a good story.

01:32:45.060 --> 01:32:45.360
Kenzo: Huh. Well, anyway.

01:32:45.360 --> 01:32:48.680
DM: This just shows why you shouldn't mess with Regemdros.

01:32:49.020 --> 01:32:49.760
Kenzo: Well, let's hear. I'm curious.

01:32:49.760 --> 01:32:51.740
DM: This is why I try and stay on her good side.

01:32:51.840 --> 01:32:52.340
Kenzo: I mean, I'm curious.

01:32:52.360 --> 01:32:53.480
DM: Look how she rewards me.

01:32:53.500 --> 01:32:55.020
Kenzo: I'm curious. Okay, go ahead.

01:32:56.780 --> 01:32:58.360
DM: These aren't my friends, just so you know.

01:32:59.060 --> 01:32:59.580
Kenzo: Okay, that's fine.

01:32:59.580 --> 01:33:01.060
DM: I want to make it clear, like, like,

01:33:01.980 --> 01:33:02.020
DM: you know, like-

01:33:02.060 --> 01:33:03.860
Kenzo: Hey, it doesn't, it, this does not [laughs]

01:33:03.860 --> 01:33:04.020
Unknown: [laughs]

01:33:04.020 --> 01:33:08.320
Kenzo: This does not in any way reflect upon your reputation or my perception of you.

01:33:08.540 --> 01:33:09.100
Kenzo: Put it that way.

01:33:09.100 --> 01:33:09.940
Unknown: [laughs]

01:33:10.020 --> 01:33:10.680
DM: Okay, so

01:33:12.480 --> 01:33:13.480
DM: a f- a friend of mine.

01:33:15.360 --> 01:33:16.160
Kenzo: Not you. A friend of yours.

01:33:16.180 --> 01:33:16.620
DM: Not me.

01:33:16.620 --> 01:33:16.880
Kenzo: Yeah, a friend.

01:33:16.880 --> 01:33:17.440
DM: A friend of mine.

01:33:17.440 --> 01:33:19.240
Wellby: Not a friend friend, but a friend.

01:33:19.320 --> 01:33:21.300
DM: Yeah. Yeah, sort of a friend.

01:33:21.400 --> 01:33:21.600
DM: Um,

01:33:22.960 --> 01:33:23.140
DM: you know,

01:33:24.300 --> 01:33:29.280
DM: his, his name was, uh [clears throat]...

01:33:29.280 --> 01:33:29.740
Kenzo: Henry. [laughs]

01:33:29.760 --> 01:33:31.640
Unknown: That's, no, that's [laughs] a good one.

01:33:31.740 --> 01:33:31.880
DM: Um,

01:33:32.920 --> 01:33:35.060
DM: um, his name was Zadar.

01:33:35.060 --> 01:33:38.960
DM: [clears throat] Uh,

01:33:39.820 --> 01:33:41.260
DM: so he told me a story once.

01:33:42.100 --> 01:33:42.740
DM: I, I, I, I...

01:33:43.900 --> 01:33:45.480
DM: Ghesh says you're collecting stories, right?

01:33:45.480 --> 01:33:46.420
DM: Here's a, here's a good one.

01:33:46.420 --> 01:33:48.780
Kenzo: I, I'm, I'm definitely, uh, I'm, I'm loving these stories.

01:33:49.780 --> 01:34:00.120
Kenzo: And by the way, by the way, too, you know, Kenza is like, kind of is like, "I, I know, I know Ghesh doesn't have a very high opinion of you," but, um, like as, as we've been talking he's been like kind of whittling like a little, a little,

01:34:00.120 --> 01:34:00.600
Kenzo: you know.

01:34:00.600 --> 01:34:00.700
DM: Yeah.

01:34:00.880 --> 01:34:10.520
Kenzo: And he makes like a really like kind of pretty, pretty like nice looking like [clears throat] thing of Ghesh and is like [clears throat], you know, "I, I'm really good at, uh, translating your stories into these, these little..."

01:34:10.580 --> 01:34:11.560
DM: Yeah, that's not bad. I like that.

01:34:11.560 --> 01:34:13.300
Kenzo: I know, I know. You know, it's just-

01:34:13.300 --> 01:34:14.600
DM: That's a good material to work with there

01:34:14.600 --> 01:34:16.620
Kenzo: ... yeah. And he just, he just tosses that to Ghesh.

01:34:16.680 --> 01:34:17.640
Kenzo: Says, "This one, that one's for you."

01:34:17.900 --> 01:34:19.420
Unknown: Oh, maybe... Can I get one?

01:34:19.960 --> 01:34:21.560
Kenzo: Oh, duh, of course. I'll make you one.

01:34:21.860 --> 01:34:23.040
Kenzo: Just keep talking. I'll make one right now.

01:34:23.040 --> 01:34:24.540
DM: So, so here's the story that Zadar told me.

01:34:25.180 --> 01:34:25.940
DM: Zadar says

01:34:27.420 --> 01:34:30.740
DM: there were some, some folks who had a plan.

01:34:30.740 --> 01:34:33.340
Unknown: [laughs]

01:34:33.380 --> 01:34:33.480
DM: Or-

01:34:33.600 --> 01:34:33.900
Unknown: A concept

01:34:33.900 --> 01:34:35.960
DM: ... maybe just a concept.

01:34:35.960 --> 01:34:39.940
DM: [laughs]

01:34:39.940 --> 01:34:40.020
Kenzo: [laughs]

01:34:40.020 --> 01:34:40.180
Unknown: [laughs]

01:34:40.220 --> 01:34:45.340
DM: And they said, and I, this is, I know this isn't true, but they believe

01:34:46.880 --> 01:34:47.640
DM: that maybe

01:34:48.860 --> 01:34:57.840
DM: there was something more than life under Regemdros and there were stories of an elder who had tales

01:34:58.900 --> 01:35:03.100
DM: of the outside world from before Regemdros arrived.

01:35:03.380 --> 01:35:03.800
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

01:35:05.940 --> 01:35:08.180
DM: And so they said, "Let's go find him."

01:35:08.800 --> 01:35:10.080
Kenzo: Hmm. Let's go find.

01:35:10.100 --> 01:35:10.260
Unknown: Wait.

01:35:10.280 --> 01:35:10.800
Kenzo: Find the elder.

01:35:10.800 --> 01:35:10.900
Unknown: There.

01:35:10.920 --> 01:35:11.740
DM: Go find the elder.

01:35:14.440 --> 01:35:15.660
DM: And they needed supplies.

01:35:15.900 --> 01:35:17.780
DM: I don't know why. That part isn't clear.

01:35:19.920 --> 01:35:20.820
DM: But they were camped,

01:35:22.220 --> 01:35:22.480
DM: uh,

01:35:24.740 --> 01:35:26.220
DM: heading towards the forest,

01:35:29.600 --> 01:35:35.340
DM: and somehow word got out that they were going to find this rumored elder who clearly doesn't exist.

01:35:37.640 --> 01:35:38.980
DM: And Regemdros came,

01:35:41.620 --> 01:35:51.680
DM: flew over their camp and burned them all to a crisp and now all that's left is a pool of acid where they used to be, and you can go visit that pool, so I know at least

01:35:51.680 --> 01:35:52.940
DM: that part's true.

01:35:52.940 --> 01:35:53.380
Kenzo: Hmm.

01:35:53.380 --> 01:35:55.460
DM: I think they were actually trying to escape the island.

01:35:57.080 --> 01:35:57.520
Kenzo: Hmm.

01:35:57.540 --> 01:36:01.859
DM: I think they were gathering supplies to escape, like go make a living somewhere else in the jungle.

01:36:04.220 --> 01:36:04.420
Unknown: Huh.

01:36:04.440 --> 01:36:07.780
DM: And they got turned into a pool of acid.

01:36:07.780 --> 01:36:10.880
DM: So unless there's another way that pools of acid can just appear,

01:36:12.460 --> 01:36:17.440
DM: my... I have never seen it, 'cause I'm like, "Why waste my time going to look at pools of acid?"

01:36:17.440 --> 01:36:20.960
DM: But my friend Zadar, he says he's seen the pool of acid and the story is.

01:36:21.240 --> 01:36:21.480
Kenzo: Huh.

01:36:22.760 --> 01:36:25.780
