Wellby: What's the thing?

01:52:08.202 --> 01:52:08.462
Delwath: Oh, yeah.

01:52:08.482 --> 01:52:09.782
Wellby: That potentially we have a wish.

01:52:10.302 --> 01:52:10.602
Delwath: Yeah.

01:52:11.622 --> 01:52:11.862
Wellby: I mean-

01:52:11.942 --> 01:52:12.082
Delwath: Like-

01:52:12.082 --> 01:52:18.102
Wellby: ... if a, if that's the sort of thing that could get her undrapped, that could be a really powerful incentive

01:52:18.102 --> 01:52:18.322
Delwath: Trade

01:52:18.842 --> 01:52:19.382
Kenzo: Oh, as a trade?

01:52:19.581 --> 01:52:19.742
Delwath: Right.

01:52:19.782 --> 01:52:20.102
Kenzo: Right.

01:52:20.182 --> 01:52:20.362
Delwath: I just-

01:52:21.022 --> 01:52:21.182
Wellby: Ooh

01:52:21.182 --> 01:52:21.242
Kenzo: Oh

01:52:21.242 --> 01:52:23.022
Wellby: ... like that could get her off the island.

01:52:23.062 --> 01:52:23.162
Delwath: Right

01:52:23.162 --> 01:52:24.162
Wellby: ... potentially.

01:52:24.162 --> 01:52:24.622
Kenzo: Maybe

