DM: Um, you hear a tu- like, uh, behind the altar you hear like a scraping stone and the

03:13:02.397 --> 03:13:11.997
DM: like so like somebody's moving a, like a, um, a stone tile, and then like climbing up you see this ancient, um,

03:13:12.997 --> 03:13:18.817
DM: elderly dragonet, like again sort of grayish, the, what you saw in scrying.

03:13:19.377 --> 03:13:20.937
DM: Um, and he's walking slowly.

03:13:20.937 --> 03:13:26.297
DM: He's carrying like a short staff in one hand and a wand in the other that he's still kind of pointing at you.

03:13:26.297 --> 03:13:27.357
Kenzo: Oh, shit.

03:13:27.397 --> 03:13:27.577
DM: Um,

03:13:30.037 --> 03:13:30.897
DM: and he says,

03:13:32.397 --> 03:13:34.997
DM: not in a booming voice anymore, um,

03:13:39.937 --> 03:13:49.417
DM: kind of blinking a little bit, "I would know the story of where you got those fragments."

03:13:50.997 --> 03:13:51.877
Kenzo: You want to know the story?

03:13:53.177 --> 03:13:54.677
DM: It seems important.

03:13:56.217 --> 03:13:59.817
DM: You say there's... Wait, did you say that you were seeking one on the island?

03:14:00.157 --> 03:14:02.457
Delwath: In our letter, but not since, not-

03:14:02.557 --> 03:14:03.697
DM: Oh, okay. Not that-

03:14:03.737 --> 03:14:03.897
Kenzo: Yes

03:14:03.897 --> 03:14:05.757
DM: ... he doesn't say anything about that.

03:14:05.757 --> 03:14:07.117
DM: He obviously didn't read the letter.

03:14:07.657 --> 03:14:12.717
Kenzo: Yeah. [laughs] Um, well,

03:14:13.597 --> 03:14:14.897
Kenzo: as I mentioned, um,

03:14:16.257 --> 03:14:17.817
Kenzo: one I've had carried with me.

03:14:18.977 --> 03:14:22.417
Kenzo: One was in, uh, what was the elvish forest thing?

03:14:22.417 --> 03:14:22.917
Kenzo: Uh.

03:14:22.937 --> 03:14:24.457
Delwath: It was in the Elderwood.

03:14:25.157 --> 03:14:26.357
Kenzo: One was in the Elderwood.

03:14:27.197 --> 03:14:28.257
Kenzo: One was with the merfolk,

03:14:29.857 --> 03:14:30.597
Kenzo: and-

03:14:30.997 --> 03:14:32.717
Unknown: Irske, in the far north.

03:14:32.717 --> 03:14:34.977
Kenzo: And one was in Irsk, in the far north.

03:14:37.797 --> 03:14:38.657
Kenzo: What do you know of this,

03:14:39.717 --> 03:14:40.417
Kenzo: these pieces?

03:14:42.217 --> 03:14:42.777
DM: Nothing.

03:14:44.157 --> 03:14:46.357
DM: I mean, I know what they are.

03:14:47.917 --> 03:14:50.557
Kenzo: You know about the other one that's here on this island?

03:14:51.657 --> 03:14:51.877
DM: No.

03:14:54.577 --> 03:14:54.837
Unknown: Really?

03:14:54.897 --> 03:14:56.717
Kenzo: Is he a- aura sense. So it's, yeah, detecting-

03:14:56.717 --> 03:14:59.317
Delwath: I'm detecting thoughts. What are his surface thoughts?

03:14:59.897 --> 03:15:00.577
Unknown: He doesn't get a save.

03:15:00.877 --> 03:15:01.197
Kenzo: Um.

03:15:02.317 --> 03:15:02.757
DM: Okay.

03:15:02.757 --> 03:15:03.177
Unknown: Worn out.

03:15:03.197 --> 03:15:05.597
DM: He's, like, super curious about...

03:15:06.697 --> 03:15:07.237
DM: Like, he's...

03:15:08.177 --> 03:15:09.737
DM: I mean, he's definitely...

03:15:09.737 --> 03:15:13.657
DM: He's, like, thinking of Rai and, like, where did these people come from?

03:15:13.657 --> 03:15:15.117
DM: Like, obviously they're...

03:15:15.677 --> 03:15:19.337
DM: I mean, like, pretty much trust that Rai wouldn't let

03:15:20.597 --> 03:15:22.857
DM: strange evil people carry around fragments of-

03:15:23.277 --> 03:15:23.577
Unknown: Right

03:15:23.577 --> 03:15:26.957
DM: ... his hand, but doesn't seem to know anything about the jade.

03:15:26.997 --> 03:15:28.317
Unknown: I mean, I, I only get, like...

03:15:28.317 --> 03:15:29.697
Unknown: Without him getting a save-

03:15:29.737 --> 03:15:29.857
DM: Yeah

03:15:29.857 --> 03:15:31.657
Delwath: ... I only get, like, basic surface thoughts.

03:15:31.677 --> 03:15:31.717
DM: Okay.

03:15:31.737 --> 03:15:32.977
Unknown: So not, like, deep motivations.

03:15:32.977 --> 03:15:35.057
Kenzo: So yeah, like, aura, aura read.

03:15:35.057 --> 03:15:37.997
Kenzo: Like, what's his, what's his deal? Is he, like, a ultra powerful...

03:15:39.477 --> 03:15:39.657
DM: No.

03:15:39.697 --> 03:15:39.877
Kenzo: Like that guy.

03:15:39.877 --> 03:15:40.877
DM: He's not ultra powerful.

03:15:41.017 --> 03:15:43.017
Kenzo: He's like a normal... What, what's his, uh, what's his-

03:15:43.077 --> 03:15:44.797
DM: Eh, he's like, you know, he's...

03:15:44.817 --> 03:15:47.757
DM: He spent, like, hundreds of years associated with Rai.

03:15:47.757 --> 03:15:49.377
DM: He's not without his tricks.

03:15:49.537 --> 03:15:49.717
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:15:50.337 --> 03:15:52.057
DM: But he's definitely weaker than you.

03:15:52.337 --> 03:15:52.517
Kenzo: Right. Right, right.

03:15:52.517 --> 03:15:54.297
DM: He'd be, like, level seven or something.

03:15:54.337 --> 03:15:55.677
Unknown: Okay. So it is Dimitaur.

03:15:56.617 --> 03:15:57.777
DM: Yeah, it's Dimitaur.

03:15:58.077 --> 03:15:58.357
Unknown: Wow.

03:16:01.157 --> 03:16:01.517
Kenzo: Um,

03:16:03.717 --> 03:16:05.817
Kenzo: yeah. There's a- another piece.

03:16:05.817 --> 03:16:07.637
Kenzo: In fact, we believe the final piece.

03:16:09.677 --> 03:16:11.537
DM: Where did they come from?

03:16:15.017 --> 03:16:15.577
Kenzo: The...

03:16:20.597 --> 03:16:22.157
Unknown: Man, where to begin with all this?

03:16:22.157 --> 03:16:24.017
Delwath: When did you last see Rai?

03:16:33.837 --> 03:16:35.037
DM: 39 years ago.

03:16:35.997 --> 03:16:36.917
Unknown: And he left to-

03:16:37.997 --> 03:16:38.737
DM: I think that's right

03:16:38.737 --> 03:16:40.177
Unknown: ... try to heal the,

03:16:42.537 --> 03:16:44.397
Delwath: the land, and you did not go with him?

03:16:48.077 --> 03:16:48.297
DM: No.

03:16:49.777 --> 03:16:51.897
Delwath: But that was... Was that the last time?

03:16:51.897 --> 03:16:52.757
DM: When he left.

03:16:53.577 --> 03:16:54.357
Kenzo: Is he still alive?

03:16:56.457 --> 03:16:56.937
DM: I mean,

03:16:58.077 --> 03:17:00.257
DM: in some sense. I don't think he can die.

03:17:03.337 --> 03:17:03.997
Kenzo: Where is he now?

03:17:06.397 --> 03:17:07.097
DM: Still in

03:17:08.357 --> 03:17:09.757
DM: Drankor, I think.

03:17:12.917 --> 03:17:13.617
DM: I don't know.

03:17:18.337 --> 03:17:22.177
Delwath: Wait, we don't know if only his hand shattered or if all of Rai shattered,

03:17:24.437 --> 03:17:24.857
Unknown: do we? Do we know?

03:17:24.877 --> 03:17:25.057
DM: No.

03:17:25.057 --> 03:17:25.577
Unknown: We don't know.

03:17:31.737 --> 03:17:35.997
Kenzo: When we found each of these pieces, we've received a vision,

03:17:37.497 --> 03:17:41.717
Kenzo: and we've been able to see the moment when his hand shattered.

03:17:42.357 --> 03:17:42.857
Kenzo: Were you there?

03:17:44.457 --> 03:17:44.837
DM: No.

03:17:46.357 --> 03:17:47.837
Unknown: No, that was when he was off trying to-

03:17:48.257 --> 03:17:48.357
Kenzo: Yeah

03:17:48.357 --> 03:17:49.077
Unknown: ... heal the-

03:17:49.637 --> 03:17:50.277
Kenzo: Yeah

03:17:50.277 --> 03:17:52.257
Delwath: ... with the awakened soul monks, right?

03:17:52.257 --> 03:17:53.217
Kenzo: Do you know about Apollyon?

03:17:58.077 --> 03:17:59.597
DM: I know the stories.

03:17:59.597 --> 03:18:00.577
DM: Many stories.

03:18:02.357 --> 03:18:04.577
Delwath: But do you know Rai was holding his prison closed?

03:18:05.177 --> 03:18:07.577
DM: Of course. What do you think?

03:18:07.597 --> 03:18:08.657
DM: I'm not stupid.

03:18:10.597 --> 03:18:11.877
DM: What is up with this Alf?

03:18:12.497 --> 03:18:13.717
Kenzo: Yeah, we deal with him.

03:18:13.717 --> 03:18:15.337
Kenzo: We manage. We just, it's...

03:18:15.337 --> 03:18:16.017
Unknown: He means well.

03:18:16.017 --> 03:18:16.237
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:18:16.237 --> 03:18:20.637
DM: [laughs]

03:18:20.677 --> 03:18:23.457
Kenzo: Um, so you understand the gravity of our quest.

03:18:24.957 --> 03:18:26.397
Kenzo: We're trying to find the last piece.

03:18:27.037 --> 03:18:28.297
DM: I don't know why.

03:18:28.297 --> 03:18:28.737
DM: I mean...

03:18:29.337 --> 03:18:31.957
Delwath: He, Rai is no longer holding Apollyon's prison closed.

03:18:32.177 --> 03:18:33.377
DM: Oh, well, that's pretty bad.

03:18:33.937 --> 03:18:34.077
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:18:34.117 --> 03:18:35.257
Unknown: Yeah. That's why, that's why-

03:18:35.257 --> 03:18:35.877
DM: So you didn't know that.

03:18:36.197 --> 03:18:38.477
Wellby: He's getting out in, like, what, 10 days?

03:18:38.477 --> 03:18:38.497
Unknown: 10 days.

03:18:38.517 --> 03:18:38.777
Kenzo: 10 days. Yeah.

03:18:38.777 --> 03:18:39.077
Wellby: Yeah.

03:18:39.097 --> 03:18:39.137
Kenzo: Yes.

03:18:39.137 --> 03:18:39.697
Wellby: So are we gonna have-

03:18:39.797 --> 03:18:40.817
DM: Oh, shit.

03:18:40.817 --> 03:18:43.997
Wellby: [laughs]

03:18:44.017 --> 03:18:44.017
DM: Rogam's gonna be pissed.

03:18:44.017 --> 03:18:44.677
Wellby: What's gonna be pissed?

03:18:44.777 --> 03:18:46.497
DM: Rogam's gonna be pissed.

03:18:46.537 --> 03:18:47.077
Kenzo: Pissed about what?

03:18:47.157 --> 03:18:48.877
Delwath: Why is Rogam's gonna be pissed?

03:18:49.497 --> 03:18:51.597
Delwath: What do you know about Rogam- Rogam'dros?

03:18:52.597 --> 03:18:53.037
DM: I mean,

03:18:54.177 --> 03:18:57.637
DM: I don't think she knows about me, and I wanna keep it that way.

03:18:57.637 --> 03:19:02.217
DM: So I only get, like, little bits and pieces of rumors.

03:19:03.977 --> 03:19:04.657
DM: Uh,

03:19:06.697 --> 03:19:07.817
DM: but, like, you know

03:19:08.977 --> 03:19:10.817
DM: Chaumut and Apollyon had a big fight, right?

03:19:11.016 --> 03:19:11.857
Kenzo: Yeah, we know about that, yeah.

03:19:11.917 --> 03:19:12.776
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

03:19:12.776 --> 03:19:14.997
DM: You know Rogam'dros is Chaumut's daughter.

03:19:15.677 --> 03:19:15.776
Unknown: What?

03:19:17.157 --> 03:19:18.297
Kenzo: What? Did not know that.

03:19:19.097 --> 03:19:19.437
DM: Some

03:19:20.457 --> 03:19:22.877
DM: task she was appointed on this island.

03:19:23.857 --> 03:19:25.097
DM: Something to guard, I think.

03:19:25.897 --> 03:19:26.957
Unknown: Something to guard.

03:19:29.597 --> 03:19:31.497
Unknown: Why do I think of Chaumut having sex?

03:19:31.497 --> 03:19:33.837
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:19:33.917 --> 03:19:35.457
DM: Who's to say dragons have-

03:19:35.677 --> 03:19:35.877
Unknown: Could, could be-

03:19:35.877 --> 03:19:36.757
DM: ... children the normal way?

03:19:36.757 --> 03:19:38.897
Kenzo: Immaculate conception. Immaculate conception.

03:19:38.897 --> 03:19:40.277
Unknown: Sure. Wow.

03:19:40.397 --> 03:19:40.977
DM: Uh.

03:19:40.997 --> 03:19:41.897
Unknown: What, what is she guarding?

03:19:42.237 --> 03:19:42.717
DM: I don't know.

03:19:43.337 --> 03:19:44.117
Unknown: It's not the jade.

03:19:45.077 --> 03:19:45.757
DM: What, no.

03:19:46.437 --> 03:19:47.717
Unknown: Because that's a more recent arrival.

03:19:47.737 --> 03:19:50.497
Wellby: I mean, could it be the island itself

03:19:51.277 --> 03:19:51.777
Wellby: somehow?

03:19:52.317 --> 03:19:56.257
Kenzo: Could it be the divine forge that Apollyon used to make the scepter of power?

03:19:56.397 --> 03:19:57.657
Wellby: Hmm, where is that, by the way?

03:20:01.337 --> 03:20:02.277
DM: Somewhere west.

03:20:03.657 --> 03:20:04.197
Kenzo: Uh.

03:20:04.237 --> 03:20:06.237
Seeker: And, and how did you...

03:20:06.257 --> 03:20:07.117
Unknown: Somewhere west on the island?

03:20:07.377 --> 03:20:08.917
Kenzo: Yeah, that's the western part of the island. It's all weird.

03:20:08.937 --> 03:20:10.117
Unknown: Yeah, the, the, the scary thing.

03:20:11.977 --> 03:20:13.977
Seeker: How did you come to stay here, Dimitaur?

03:20:14.637 --> 03:20:15.477
Kenzo: Oh, we don't know his name yet.

03:20:15.797 --> 03:20:15.937
Unknown: Oh,

03:20:17.457 --> 03:20:21.057
Unknown: I thought, I thought we confirmed the name earlier.

03:20:21.057 --> 03:20:21.917
DM: That was out of game.

03:20:21.957 --> 03:20:22.217
Unknown: Yeah.

03:20:23.057 --> 03:20:23.477
DM: You can ask his name in game.

03:20:23.477 --> 03:20:25.137
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah. Actually, yeah. What, what is your name?

03:20:25.457 --> 03:20:26.077
DM: Dimitaur.

03:20:26.677 --> 03:20:26.997
Kenzo: Huh.

03:20:28.617 --> 03:20:29.557
Unknown: How did you come to stay here?

03:20:30.177 --> 03:20:30.377
DM: Well,

03:20:33.297 --> 03:20:34.277
DM: Rai never came back.

03:20:35.877 --> 03:20:36.277
Kenzo: Back here?

03:20:38.857 --> 03:20:42.717
DM: Back to where we were in Drankor keeping watch over Apollyon.

03:20:43.357 --> 03:20:44.517
Kenzo: Hmm.

03:20:44.537 --> 03:20:45.897
DM: I knew he had trained here.

03:20:49.797 --> 03:20:50.117
DM: I thought,

03:20:52.097 --> 03:20:52.697
DM: let's see.

03:20:54.637 --> 03:20:55.557
Kenzo: How long have you been here now?

03:20:57.317 --> 03:20:59.889
DM: Like...

03:20:59.889 --> 03:21:00.889
DM: 35 years

03:21:01.849 --> 03:21:02.869
Kenzo: Are you waiting for Rai here?

03:21:06.409 --> 03:21:08.569
DM: Well, I didn't know so many of my people lived here.

03:21:09.989 --> 03:21:10.949
DM: Now I'm kind of...

03:21:11.829 --> 03:21:12.629
DM: I don't know what to do.

03:21:15.369 --> 03:21:15.469
Kenzo: Hmm.

03:21:16.769 --> 03:21:19.089
Seeker: What's your relationship like with, with the Dragonets?

03:21:21.549 --> 03:21:24.869
DM: I'm pretty sure Ra'ghemdros would kill me if she knew I was here.

03:21:25.629 --> 03:21:25.889
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

03:21:26.509 --> 03:21:32.369
DM: So I don't really talk to them much, but some of them come find me secretly.

03:21:33.809 --> 03:21:36.909
Seeker: Do you think you could enlist them to help us?

03:21:37.669 --> 03:21:38.649
DM: Help you do what?

03:21:40.229 --> 03:21:42.709
Seeker: We're trying to figure that out, but we need to get that jade.

03:21:42.809 --> 03:21:43.329
DM: Ah,

03:21:44.169 --> 03:21:45.249
DM: planners, I see.

03:21:45.249 --> 03:21:48.369
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:21:48.409 --> 03:21:49.329
Unknown: Planners, I see.

03:21:49.349 --> 03:21:51.049
Kenzo: Does he say that with contempt or [laughs]

03:21:51.149 --> 03:21:52.289
DM: A little bit with contempt.

03:21:52.989 --> 03:21:54.269
Kenzo: I... We, we don't plan that much.

03:21:54.509 --> 03:21:55.349
Kenzo: Don't worry. Um,

03:21:57.129 --> 03:21:57.689
Kenzo: so you say-

03:21:58.409 --> 03:22:00.969
DM: The important thing is to just not keep the plans you make.

03:22:01.249 --> 03:22:01.669
Kenzo: Heh, we never do that.

03:22:01.689 --> 03:22:03.469
Wellby: Yeah, we do. Yeah, yeah. Right.

03:22:03.469 --> 03:22:03.668
Kenzo: So

03:22:05.429 --> 03:22:10.109
Kenzo: the dragon, uh, is she, is she free?

03:22:10.849 --> 03:22:13.309
Kenzo: We had a feeling she may also be captive.

03:22:15.849 --> 03:22:15.909
DM: Eh.

03:22:15.909 --> 03:22:16.849
Kenzo: Can she travel freely?

03:22:19.069 --> 03:22:19.769
DM: You mean, like-

03:22:20.189 --> 03:22:21.009
Kenzo: Can she leave her lair?

03:22:21.669 --> 03:22:22.369
DM: Yeah.

03:22:24.269 --> 03:22:24.689
DM: Is that...

03:22:27.529 --> 03:22:29.489
DM: Where did you get this idea from?

03:22:29.629 --> 03:22:29.709
Kenzo: Uh.

03:22:31.029 --> 03:22:33.989
DM: I mean, do you know many dragons that don't leave their lairs?

03:22:34.569 --> 03:22:36.449
Delwath: She hasn't seen too much

03:22:37.329 --> 03:22:38.909
Delwath: according to the Dragonets down there.

03:22:39.529 --> 03:22:40.829
DM: Well, she has some task.

03:22:41.689 --> 03:22:42.989
DM: Maybe it's too important.

03:22:42.989 --> 03:22:43.489
DM: I don't know.

03:22:45.649 --> 03:22:47.849
Seeker: An important task underground?

03:22:51.869 --> 03:22:54.729
DM: I'm not here to solve your problems, guys.

03:22:54.729 --> 03:22:56.489
Wellby: [laughs]

03:22:56.489 --> 03:22:57.569
Unknown: Well, what can we do to help you?

03:22:57.569 --> 03:23:04.789
DM: [coughs] Wait, you want to help me?

03:23:04.789 --> 03:23:05.069
Unknown: Yeah.

03:23:08.869 --> 03:23:09.369
DM: Well, um,

03:23:11.949 --> 03:23:14.409
DM: something more interesting to eat would be nice.

03:23:15.829 --> 03:23:16.889
Kenzo: We can help you with that.

03:23:16.889 --> 03:23:18.389
Wellby: We've got these berries. They're pretty good.

03:23:20.229 --> 03:23:21.949
DM: Oh, well, fruit's easy.

03:23:22.849 --> 03:23:24.029
DM: My circles make it.

03:23:24.729 --> 03:23:26.409
Delwath: Hmm. I'll send the...

03:23:26.409 --> 03:23:28.389
Delwath: my lynxes out to go collect some food.

03:23:29.049 --> 03:23:30.449
Kenzo: I can make you a meal, Dimitar.

03:23:30.449 --> 03:23:32.929
Seeker: I suppose this runic food gets a little old

03:23:33.829 --> 03:23:33.909
Unknown: day in and day out.

03:23:33.929 --> 03:23:36.169
DM: Yeah, it's like 12 menu choices.

03:23:37.049 --> 03:23:37.469
Kenzo: That's...

03:23:38.089 --> 03:23:39.349
DM: You gotta go out there. There's...

03:23:39.369 --> 03:23:42.369
DM: The biggest thing is none of the ones up here are seafood.

03:23:43.469 --> 03:23:43.869
Kenzo: Ah.

03:23:43.989 --> 03:23:48.449
Seeker: Of course, you like a little seafood once in a while, but it's hard to get down there 'cause of all the other Dragonets, so...

03:23:49.509 --> 03:23:51.269
DM: Also, you know, at my age,

03:23:52.029 --> 03:23:54.549
DM: I'm not as agile as I once was in the air.

03:23:54.829 --> 03:23:55.369
Unknown: Hmm.

03:23:55.369 --> 03:23:56.089
Kenzo: Hmm. Yeah.

03:23:56.149 --> 03:23:57.249
Unknown: Of course. Of course.

03:23:57.429 --> 03:23:57.549
Kenzo: Yeah. Hmm.

03:23:59.769 --> 03:24:01.869
Kenzo: Uh, so just so you know,

03:24:03.449 --> 03:24:04.669
Kenzo: this is our plan.

03:24:04.669 --> 03:24:07.569
Kenzo: I know you're not, you know, but just curious your thoughts on it.

03:24:07.569 --> 03:24:10.429
Kenzo: We, uh, want to get that last piece of jade.

03:24:12.049 --> 03:24:17.329
Kenzo: Um, I think when we put those pieces together, um, you know, I mentioned I got a...

03:24:17.329 --> 03:24:21.629
Kenzo: been getting a vision of, of Rai basically every time we find one of these pieces of jade.

03:24:23.469 --> 03:24:23.789
Kenzo: Um,

03:24:25.169 --> 03:24:25.609
Kenzo: we

03:24:26.629 --> 03:24:30.489
Kenzo: suspect at least that once we get the final piece together,

03:24:31.889 --> 03:24:36.189
Kenzo: we're gonna get a pretty important piece of information about where Apollyon is,

03:24:37.749 --> 03:24:39.629
Kenzo: um, storing himself,

03:24:41.109 --> 03:24:43.249
Kenzo: and probably in Drankor someplace.

03:24:43.249 --> 03:24:43.829
DM: Where-

03:24:43.869 --> 03:24:44.569
Kenzo: Probably gonna have to go in.

03:24:44.569 --> 03:24:46.109
DM: Wait, you don't know that already?

03:24:46.889 --> 03:24:47.129
Kenzo: Do you know?

03:24:47.149 --> 03:24:48.589
DM: You haven't, like, scouted?

03:24:48.589 --> 03:24:49.689
Kenzo: We haven't been to Drankor yet, no.

03:24:50.209 --> 03:24:51.809
DM: His tomb is pretty obvious.

03:24:51.949 --> 03:24:52.089
Kenzo: Yeah?

03:24:53.069 --> 03:24:55.069
Delwath: But his tomb is not where his, uh-

03:24:55.569 --> 03:24:56.029
Wellby: Phylactery is

03:24:56.029 --> 03:24:56.809
Unknown: ... phylactery is.

03:24:57.969 --> 03:24:58.429
Unknown: That would be pretty tough.

03:24:58.429 --> 03:24:59.769
DM: Oh, you want to kill him,

03:25:01.149 --> 03:25:02.189
DM: not just lock him up?

03:25:03.429 --> 03:25:03.749
Unknown: If you can.

03:25:03.789 --> 03:25:04.989
Wellby: Yeah, how would we lock him up?

03:25:05.569 --> 03:25:07.049
DM: I don't know. Retie the knots.

03:25:07.069 --> 03:25:07.889
DM: Aren't you magic?

03:25:08.409 --> 03:25:09.329
Kenzo: Eh, not that way.

03:25:09.749 --> 03:25:09.849
Wellby: Yeah, no.

03:25:09.849 --> 03:25:11.129
Kenzo: I mean, maybe Rai could help us.

03:25:14.129 --> 03:25:15.908
DM: Oh, well, that's much harder.

03:25:16.489 --> 03:25:17.209
Kenzo: Why is that much harder?

03:25:17.648 --> 03:25:19.449
DM: Well, I don't know where his phylactery is.

03:25:19.929 --> 03:25:23.069
Kenzo: I... But, well, that's why we get the last piece of jade and then we figure out where the phylactery is.

03:25:23.069 --> 03:25:24.669
Unknown: [laughs] Have you been listening to our story?

03:25:24.749 --> 03:25:26.789
DM: Oh, you think Rai knows where his phylactery is?

03:25:27.329 --> 03:25:28.609
DM: Oh, maybe he does, actually.

03:25:30.889 --> 03:25:31.129
DM: Hmm.

03:25:32.649 --> 03:25:33.449
DM: Interesting.

03:25:33.449 --> 03:25:34.549
Kenzo: Can you help us find Rai?

03:25:36.309 --> 03:25:36.869
DM: I looked.

03:25:38.089 --> 03:25:39.349
Kenzo: Yeah, in Drankor, huh? Couldn't find him.

03:25:39.349 --> 03:25:40.049
DM: He never came back.

03:25:40.669 --> 03:25:40.949
Wellby: Hmm.

03:25:42.049 --> 03:25:43.149
DM: He went off with the monks.

03:25:46.049 --> 03:25:46.149
Wellby: Oh, the monks.

03:25:46.149 --> 03:25:48.629
DM: Wait, that was your friends who convinced him to do that?

03:25:50.389 --> 03:25:52.389
Kenzo: I think Rai was the one that was convincing them.

03:25:53.129 --> 03:25:54.129
DM: Oh, that's possible.

03:25:54.209 --> 03:25:54.369
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:25:54.369 --> 03:25:55.369
Wellby: [laughs]

03:25:55.409 --> 03:25:56.849
Kenzo: The other way around with the convincing.

03:25:57.649 --> 03:26:00.529
DM: I know he did. Like, they had a few little successes.

03:26:01.409 --> 03:26:02.249
Kenzo: Successes doing what?

03:26:03.029 --> 03:26:04.609
DM: Cleaning up the Seeds of Chaos.

03:26:05.009 --> 03:26:05.289
Unknown: Right.

03:26:05.849 --> 03:26:06.129
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:26:07.169 --> 03:26:08.309
DM: Then they went for the big one.

03:26:09.949 --> 03:26:10.929
DM: I thought it was a mistake.

03:26:12.109 --> 03:26:13.169
Kenzo: Does Cha'mut have other children?

03:26:13.589 --> 03:26:14.249
Unknown: If only he'd listened.

03:26:15.409 --> 03:26:16.829
DM: Yeah, if only Rai... Rai never...

03:26:17.689 --> 03:26:18.749
DM: He didn't listen to me.

03:26:19.809 --> 03:26:20.249
DM: Damn it.

03:26:21.009 --> 03:26:22.909
Kenzo: What, what, what, what, what was your advice to Rai?

03:26:22.929 --> 03:26:23.749
Kenzo: What were you trying to get him to do?

03:26:23.809 --> 03:26:29.469
DM: Don't go to the gi- the biggest, giantest Seed of Chaos and try and fix it in Isingue.

03:26:29.469 --> 03:26:31.189
DM: That seems like a stupid thing to do.

03:26:33.629 --> 03:26:35.869
Seeker: That's how all those, those monks were lost, presumably.

03:26:35.889 --> 03:26:35.909
DM: Mm.

03:26:37.029 --> 03:26:40.729
Delwath: Remember, that's the acidic ooze that we flew over.

03:26:40.729 --> 03:26:41.089
Kenzo: What is?

03:26:42.369 --> 03:26:42.369
DM: Oh.

03:26:45.709 --> 03:26:45.749
Kenzo: Oh.

03:26:45.749 --> 03:26:47.129
Wellby: Yeah. No, I think you were right.

03:26:47.129 --> 03:26:48.829
Unknown: [laughs] Dimitar's-

03:26:48.889 --> 03:26:49.949
DM: This one's smart

03:26:49.949 --> 03:26:51.949
Seeker: ... Dimitar's got some insights into how the world works.

03:26:52.309 --> 03:26:55.149
Delwath: But maybe after we kill Apollyon we should go figure it out.

03:26:56.589 --> 03:26:58.689
Seeker: Well, we should see what Dimitar says about that.

03:26:58.729 --> 03:27:00.689
Kenzo: Yeah. Wait, but, yeah, but, but what were you trying to tell Rai?

03:27:00.689 --> 03:27:02.909
Unknown: So your, your, your advice to Rai was-

03:27:03.169 --> 03:27:04.389
Unknown: It did hurt our ship after all

03:27:04.389 --> 03:27:06.329
DM: ... don't go. It's the biggest place of all.

03:27:06.349 --> 03:27:07.389
Unknown: We gotta take revenge

03:27:09.245 --> 03:27:09.585
Unknown: It's true.

03:27:09.645 --> 03:27:11.205
DM: But he was pretty sure he could do it.

03:27:11.645 --> 03:27:11.865
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:27:13.325 --> 03:27:13.525
Unknown: Huh.

03:27:15.085 --> 03:27:15.405
Kenzo: Um,

03:27:16.625 --> 03:27:17.485
Kenzo: Shemut has other children?

03:27:18.345 --> 03:27:18.805
DM: I don't know.

03:27:19.505 --> 03:27:20.645
Kenzo: How do you know this is Shemut's daughter?

03:27:22.685 --> 03:27:24.525
Unknown: You haven't heard her brag?

03:27:25.525 --> 03:27:25.965
Kenzo: What's brag?

03:27:26.985 --> 03:27:28.385
Unknown: When did you talk to her?

03:27:29.325 --> 03:27:31.345
DM: I didn't talk to her. You didn't ask it.

03:27:31.985 --> 03:27:33.565
DM: You just never bothered to ask.

03:27:33.585 --> 03:27:33.625
DM: Like-

03:27:33.685 --> 03:27:34.125
Kenzo: Ask who?

03:27:34.505 --> 03:27:37.205
DM: Any of the stupid dragonets flying around.

03:27:38.205 --> 03:27:39.865
DM: I am... He's, like, imitating somebody.

03:27:40.685 --> 03:27:43.365
DM: I am Ra'ghemdros, daughter of Shemut.

03:27:43.385 --> 03:27:50.025
DM: I am the Light Stealer and the Final Shadow, the Devourer of Drankor, known as the Eternal Night.

03:27:50.505 --> 03:27:51.965
DM: She's not shy about it.

03:27:52.165 --> 03:27:53.105
Kenzo: She's pretty boastful, huh?

03:27:53.545 --> 03:27:54.705
Unknown: Those are some good names though.

03:27:55.285 --> 03:27:55.545
Kenzo: Yeah?

03:27:56.265 --> 03:27:58.385
Unknown: Uh, we haven't seen the ending though.

03:27:58.485 --> 03:28:00.205
Kenzo: Yeah, we have. We just, we just haven't been there that long.

03:28:00.205 --> 03:28:04.225
Kenzo: We've only been here for half a day. So, so okay, so she's Shemut's daughter.

03:28:04.225 --> 03:28:06.205
Kenzo: She's here on some task that Shemut

03:28:07.445 --> 03:28:08.185
Kenzo: has put her to.

03:28:08.905 --> 03:28:09.045
Unknown: Right.

03:28:09.045 --> 03:28:09.585
Kenzo: Nominally.

03:28:09.665 --> 03:28:09.825
DM: Yep.

03:28:11.365 --> 03:28:13.945
Kenzo: And you don't know what that task is.

03:28:14.965 --> 03:28:17.185
Delwath: Hey, did the hobgoblin wizard who's in the...

03:28:17.185 --> 03:28:18.365
Unknown: She was against Shemut, right?

03:28:18.465 --> 03:28:19.365
DM: Yeah.

03:28:19.365 --> 03:28:21.885
Delwath: You know who might be an ally killing Shemut's daughter?

03:28:24.185 --> 03:28:26.105
Seeker: Is the hobgoblin wi- wizard we have trapped in the mirror?

03:28:26.185 --> 03:28:26.425
Unknown: Yeah.

03:28:26.425 --> 03:28:26.645
DM: Yeah.

03:28:26.805 --> 03:28:29.165
Wellby: She's not gonna go back in the mirror again after what's happened.

03:28:29.225 --> 03:28:30.085
DM: No, of course not.

03:28:30.445 --> 03:28:32.765
Seeker: No, her... What she gets in re- in return is...

03:28:33.345 --> 03:28:34.625
Unknown: Well, no, we can't give her the island.

03:28:36.805 --> 03:28:39.285
Wellby: We can't exactly stop her from taking [laughs].

03:28:39.285 --> 03:28:40.825
Delwath: We could, we could try to kill her though.

03:28:42.305 --> 03:28:42.445
Unknown: Hm.

03:28:42.445 --> 03:28:43.225
DM: Double cross her.

03:28:44.285 --> 03:28:44.925
DM: Maybe a bad idea.

03:28:45.005 --> 03:28:46.205
Unknown: I, yeah, that's-

03:28:46.245 --> 03:28:47.505
DM: But, like, there's something here.

03:28:48.345 --> 03:28:48.525
Kenzo: Okay.

03:28:48.525 --> 03:28:49.785
Unknown: But she was an ally of Shemut?

03:28:49.905 --> 03:28:50.285
DM: Enemy.

03:28:50.505 --> 03:28:50.505
Kenzo: Enemy.

03:28:50.525 --> 03:28:52.025
DM: But she was trapped by...

03:28:52.025 --> 03:28:56.185
DM: She tried to trap Shemut in the mirror, and he was like, "No, no, no, you go in the mirror."

03:28:56.225 --> 03:28:56.345
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:28:56.405 --> 03:28:58.805
Wellby: Oh, maybe we could s- maybe she knows about Ra'ghemdros.

03:28:59.505 --> 03:29:00.425
DM: We could talk to her.

03:29:01.125 --> 03:29:01.905
Unknown: That'd be a great person to talk to.

03:29:01.965 --> 03:29:02.645
Unknown: I think it's a good idea.

03:29:03.105 --> 03:29:03.125
Unknown: Yeah.

03:29:03.145 --> 03:29:03.785
Unknown: I think it's a good idea.

03:29:05.185 --> 03:29:05.765
Kenzo: Yeah, uh-

03:29:05.865 --> 03:29:09.545
Delwath: She might help us just to see Ra'ghemdros die, even in not being freed.

03:29:09.665 --> 03:29:17.565
Wellby: But also, what if she's been biding her time this entire time, and, like, could have left the prison at any moment, and now we take her out and talk to her and-

03:29:18.245 --> 03:29:19.485
Unknown: We're not taking her out to talk to her.

03:29:19.525 --> 03:29:20.585
Unknown: We're talking to her in the mirror.

03:29:20.585 --> 03:29:20.645
DM: No, we can talk to her in the mirror.

03:29:20.685 --> 03:29:21.705
Unknown: Hm.

03:29:21.785 --> 03:29:22.885
DM: I, I think we should talk to her.

03:29:22.925 --> 03:29:25.745
Kenzo: Hold on, hold on. But let's just... We're, th- we're talking to Dimitaur now, right?

03:29:25.765 --> 03:29:27.605
Kenzo: So what else do we do- want to learn from Dimitaur?

03:29:31.205 --> 03:29:32.605
Kenzo: Can you help us find Rai

03:29:34.045 --> 03:29:42.705
Kenzo: now? 'Cause we're going to Drankor next after this, almost certainly.

03:29:44.585 --> 03:29:46.585
DM: I do not wanna go back to Drankor.

03:29:46.585 --> 03:29:47.625
DM: [coughs]

03:29:47.625 --> 03:29:49.325
Delwath: But you know it pretty well.

03:29:52.065 --> 03:29:52.585
DM: I do.

03:29:53.385 --> 03:29:53.625
Unknown: Okay.

03:29:54.025 --> 03:29:55.605
Kenzo: One favor.

03:29:55.605 --> 03:29:56.985
Kenzo: Maybe you can help us with a map.

03:29:57.005 --> 03:29:59.285
Delwath: Hm. I was gonna say, can we spend, like, two hours

03:30:00.625 --> 03:30:03.205
Delwath: digging through everything he knows about Drankor?

03:30:03.225 --> 03:30:06.005
DM: You can, but you can't hear it now because I haven't made it up.

03:30:06.005 --> 03:30:07.325
Unknown: Yes, I know. That's what I was just gonna say.

03:30:07.465 --> 03:30:07.905
Kenzo: That's fine.

03:30:09.105 --> 03:30:09.665
DM: Um-

03:30:10.425 --> 03:30:15.685
Delwath: I mean, would he... What, why don't we just, like, c- c- could you tell us everything you know?

03:30:17.825 --> 03:30:19.305
DM: Yeah, I could tell you some stuff.

03:30:19.945 --> 03:30:21.185
Kenzo: Look, here's the basics.

03:30:22.025 --> 03:30:23.745
Kenzo: We get the last piece of jade.

03:30:23.745 --> 03:30:26.105
Kenzo: Hopefully, that tells us where the phylactery is.

03:30:26.105 --> 03:30:30.165
Kenzo: Almost certainly it's gonna be in Drankor, and then we're gonna go and try and destroy the phylactery.

03:30:30.165 --> 03:30:32.425
Kenzo: We expect it's gonna be really hard going there.

03:30:32.425 --> 03:30:36.505
Kenzo: Is Drankor now, like, is it, like, some haunted, like, fucked up place that's gonna, like, try to kill us at every turn?

03:30:39.485 --> 03:30:41.685
DM: It wasn't really like that when Rai was there.

03:30:42.965 --> 03:30:44.365
DM: I bet it's gotten a lot worse.

03:30:44.885 --> 03:30:45.385
Kenzo: Since when?

03:30:45.725 --> 03:30:46.365
Unknown: Since Rai left.

03:30:46.865 --> 03:30:47.505
DM: Since Rai left.

03:30:47.545 --> 03:30:48.365
Kenzo: Like 39 years ago?

03:30:48.565 --> 03:30:48.745
Unknown: Yeah.

03:30:48.765 --> 03:30:48.765
DM: Yeah.

03:30:48.825 --> 03:30:49.465
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:30:49.605 --> 03:30:50.945
DM: I couldn't stay much,

03:30:51.945 --> 03:30:54.265
DM: like, only a few months.

03:30:54.805 --> 03:31:05.005
DM: I only stayed there a few months waiting for him, and it got dark and scary, and there was this, like, aura of fear that radiated out through the whole place coming

03:31:05.005 --> 03:31:09.425
DM: from Apollyon's tomb. And every morning, I woke up wanting to run away, and eventually I did.

03:31:09.685 --> 03:31:09.905
Kenzo: Hm.

03:31:09.925 --> 03:31:11.665
DM: And I'm not sure I could go back.

03:31:12.185 --> 03:31:13.645
Kenzo: Yeah, it doesn't sound like a good place.

03:31:15.645 --> 03:31:15.905
Kenzo: Um-

03:31:18.305 --> 03:31:20.325
Delwath: Collect immunity to fear artifacts.

03:31:20.925 --> 03:31:21.965
Kenzo: Or a feast.

03:31:23.085 --> 03:31:23.745
Unknown: I think one of the binding-

03:31:23.765 --> 03:31:24.225
Unknown: Or Rizwin

03:31:24.225 --> 03:31:24.625
Unknown: ... things can

03:31:25.625 --> 03:31:27.425
Unknown: be Rizwin. Or Rizwin.

03:31:27.465 --> 03:31:29.024
Seeker: I wonder how Rizwin's doing. Oh, well.

03:31:29.065 --> 03:31:30.005
Kenzo: So, so-

03:31:30.024 --> 03:31:30.405
Unknown: Who knows?

03:31:31.125 --> 03:31:35.385
Kenzo: Okay. Anyways, yeah, we appreciate any insights you have 'cause I think we're gonna have to go there.

03:31:35.385 --> 03:31:37.545
Kenzo: It sounds pretty scary, but we are gonna try to go there.

03:31:38.065 --> 03:31:42.705
Kenzo: And when we go there, if Rai is still there, if, do you have any tips on if we wanna try to find him?

03:31:46.645 --> 03:31:47.765
Kenzo: Would you want, would you want his hand back?

03:31:49.785 --> 03:31:50.205
DM: I mean,

03:31:52.545 --> 03:31:55.465
DM: if I took your hand from you and then showed up, would you want it back?

03:31:56.985 --> 03:31:57.745
Kenzo: How do we give it back to him?

03:31:58.345 --> 03:32:01.745
DM: I don't know. Like, maybe you could take it and hand it to him.

03:32:02.385 --> 03:32:03.185
Unknown: Hand it to him?

03:32:03.225 --> 03:32:03.725
Kenzo: Here he is.

03:32:04.405 --> 03:32:05.365
DM: This one's got it.

03:32:05.645 --> 03:32:06.045
Unknown: Nice.

03:32:06.445 --> 03:32:07.785
Kenzo: So, so, so-

03:32:07.845 --> 03:32:08.225
Unknown: Nice

03:32:08.225 --> 03:32:10.605
Kenzo: ... but yeah, but do you, any, any, any ideas how to find him?

03:32:12.365 --> 03:32:13.785
Unknown: Do, do we even know he's findable?

03:32:13.785 --> 03:32:14.465
Unknown: I mean, we don't actually-

03:32:14.565 --> 03:32:15.745
Kenzo: We're asking. I mean, I don't know.

03:32:15.805 --> 03:32:17.145
Unknown: Didn't Dimitaur say that-

03:32:17.165 --> 03:32:19.585
Kenzo: Would we even know if he was dead? No, he said he d- can't ever die.

03:32:19.585 --> 03:32:20.445
Kenzo: The part is something, somewhere-

03:32:20.485 --> 03:32:25.125
Delwath: I mean, he said he couldn't find him and he went looking, and he also said he doesn't think Rai can ever die.

03:32:25.305 --> 03:32:28.345
DM: But he wasn't in... Dimitaur could not find him in Drankor.

03:32:28.405 --> 03:32:28.585
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:32:29.105 --> 03:32:32.865
DM: Maybe he was, like, trapped for a while and then came back to Drankor somehow.

03:32:32.885 --> 03:32:42.465
Kenzo: But what, what I'm trying to say is when you're, when you're looking for some kind of weird, you know, immortal sorcerer or whatever, like, does he respond to anything or, like, is there anything that-

03:32:42.485 --> 03:32:44.805
DM: I don't know. Send your, like, spirit dog after him.

03:32:45.825 --> 03:32:47.105
Kenzo: Is that what you try to do when you find him?

03:32:47.125 --> 03:32:47.985
Kenzo: Like, what do you do when you try to find him?

03:32:47.985 --> 03:32:50.425
Delwath: Actually, that's not a bad idea. Why didn't we think of that?

03:32:50.425 --> 03:32:52.445
Unknown: [laughs]

03:32:52.465 --> 03:32:54.665
DM: I don't know. You're just not as smart as he, I guess.

03:32:54.785 --> 03:32:58.605
Kenzo: I mean, we're clearly not, but, like, any, any other tips, any other advice for, for finding him?

03:33:01.305 --> 03:33:01.785
DM: I mean,

03:33:03.085 --> 03:33:05.485
DM: the last place I know he was was Isingay.

03:33:06.805 --> 03:33:07.385
Kenzo: Isingay?

03:33:07.985 --> 03:33:09.105
Unknown: That's where that acidic ooze is

03:33:10.025 --> 03:33:10.305
Kenzo: Huh?

03:33:10.385 --> 03:33:11.765
Unknown: When we're all... The whole...

03:33:11.785 --> 03:33:11.905
Unknown: It was like-

03:33:11.945 --> 03:33:15.625
Delwath: Remember we flew, we flew over Isingue in Vincharna.

03:33:15.685 --> 03:33:15.845
Unknown: Yeah.

03:33:15.885 --> 03:33:19.825
Delwath: And we went down to investigate 'cause it looked cool, and a tendril of acidic ooze-

03:33:19.845 --> 03:33:20.545
Unknown: Yes, totally. I totally remember that

03:33:20.545 --> 03:33:21.085
DM: Punched a hole in the-

03:33:21.125 --> 03:33:22.405
Unknown: That's the last place where I was?

03:33:22.505 --> 03:33:23.585
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:33:23.645 --> 03:33:25.165
DM: That's when we went with the monks to try and-

03:33:25.205 --> 03:33:27.825
Delwath: That is apparently where he was trying to heal the land.

03:33:27.825 --> 03:33:29.525
Delwath: That's the seat of chaos. He was trying to get rid of it.

03:33:29.525 --> 03:33:31.285
Seeker: So that was a portal or something.

03:33:31.285 --> 03:33:31.785
Kenzo: Fuck.

03:33:31.785 --> 03:33:35.265
Seeker: But, and all those monks basically died or didn't come back anyway.

03:33:35.265 --> 03:33:39.005
DM: They either died or they got scattered around the planes when they were...

03:33:40.145 --> 03:33:41.345
DM: when the chaos happened.

03:33:47.765 --> 03:33:49.845
Wellby: What do you, what do you think the odds are of killing that dragon?

03:33:55.245 --> 03:33:55.885
DM: I couldn't.

03:33:56.785 --> 03:33:57.285
DM: I don't know.

03:33:58.705 --> 03:34:00.965
DM: You're, like, not too shabby from what I've seen.

03:34:04.125 --> 03:34:06.985
DM: I mean, you certainly avoided my trap neatly.

03:34:06.985 --> 03:34:12.485
DM: [sighs] But, like...

03:34:12.485 --> 03:34:14.305
Seeker: What would it take to lure her out of her lair, though?

03:34:14.365 --> 03:34:15.285
Wellby: Yeah. What would get her out?

03:34:15.305 --> 03:34:16.585
Kenzo: Yeah. We, we don't want to fight her in there.

03:34:16.865 --> 03:34:19.785
Seeker: We've heard that she l-loves shiny things.

03:34:21.205 --> 03:34:21.625
DM: Yeah.

03:34:23.025 --> 03:34:24.845
Kenzo: But [coughs]...

03:34:24.905 --> 03:34:27.265
Wellby: Why would she kill you if she knew you were on the island?

03:34:29.425 --> 03:34:32.005
Wellby: 'Cause of your, like, escape attempt that you led?

03:34:32.745 --> 03:34:34.145
Kenzo: Bad influence on the other dragonets.

03:34:34.285 --> 03:34:35.985
DM: Yeah. She thinks I'm a bad influence.

03:34:35.985 --> 03:34:39.685
Delwath: I mean, she might have a hatred of Rai who killed her father.

03:34:40.485 --> 03:34:41.125
Wellby: Yeah, that's fair.

03:34:43.145 --> 03:34:49.045
DM: I think she just likes her little simple empire here.

03:34:50.505 --> 03:34:53.045
DM: She doesn't like anybody who kinda

03:34:55.025 --> 03:34:55.765
DM: speaks up.

03:34:56.385 --> 03:34:57.445
Unknown: So you're saying her, um,

03:34:58.525 --> 03:35:01.125
Seeker: ambitions aren't as grandiose as Cha'mutte's.

03:35:03.865 --> 03:35:07.045
DM: I see no reason why she couldn't leave this island if she wanted to.

03:35:07.625 --> 03:35:12.525
Kenzo: So she's s- she's serving some kind of function here that's useful, of use to her deceased dad.

03:35:16.005 --> 03:35:19.385
Kenzo: Um, if you were us and, uh,

03:35:20.585 --> 03:35:21.145
Kenzo: you needed to

03:35:22.445 --> 03:35:23.945
Kenzo: get that piece of jade back from the dragon,

03:35:24.985 --> 03:35:25.505
Kenzo: any advice?

03:35:31.585 --> 03:35:32.745
DM: If I were you?

03:35:32.845 --> 03:35:33.105
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:35:35.405 --> 03:35:36.785
DM: I'd pick an easier quest.

03:35:37.745 --> 03:35:38.325
Kenzo: Eh.

03:35:39.445 --> 03:35:40.725
Kenzo: Let's say you had to do this one, though.

03:35:40.725 --> 03:35:42.345
DM: [laughs] Good.

03:35:46.205 --> 03:35:46.365
DM: [laughs]

03:35:46.505 --> 03:35:47.625
Unknown: Oh, Dimitar.

03:35:47.985 --> 03:35:48.525
Kenzo: Does, um,

03:35:50.025 --> 03:35:51.645
Delwath: she keep her deals for the most part?

03:35:52.985 --> 03:35:53.225
DM: Yeah.

03:35:56.705 --> 03:35:57.445
Kenzo: You think she would trade?

03:35:58.985 --> 03:36:03.965
DM: She might. I mean, she might just, like, say, "I'll kill you and take your stuff anyway."

03:36:04.965 --> 03:36:06.165
Kenzo: But that'd be fine with us.

03:36:06.165 --> 03:36:06.725
Wellby: That's okay.

03:36:06.725 --> 03:36:08.585
Delwath: Isn't that kind of the opposite of keeping your deals?

03:36:10.725 --> 03:36:18.245
DM: Uh... [laughs]

03:36:18.245 --> 03:36:18.305
Unknown: [laughs]

03:36:18.405 --> 03:36:19.305
DM: She-

03:36:19.305 --> 03:36:20.885
Unknown: When you said yes, did you mean no?

03:36:20.885 --> 03:36:21.385
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:36:21.385 --> 03:36:22.005
DM: No, no, no, no, no.

03:36:22.385 --> 03:36:22.445
Kenzo: No.

03:36:22.445 --> 03:36:27.165
DM: She's never, uh, she's never taken away a tower she gave to a dragonet.

03:36:27.865 --> 03:36:28.065
Kenzo: Hm.

03:36:30.325 --> 03:36:31.845
DM: But, you know,

03:36:34.725 --> 03:36:40.665
DM: who knows? Many of them might go in there and be like, "Hey, here's some stuff," and she says, "I don't like you, so I'll just take that stuff."

03:36:41.305 --> 03:36:44.765
Seeker: And she sometimes kills them to prove a point or to make an example of them.

03:36:45.305 --> 03:36:46.605
DM: Yeah, sometimes. I mean,

03:36:47.965 --> 03:36:49.605
DM: gotta keep a little bit of an aura of fear.

03:36:54.945 --> 03:36:56.185
Unknown: But she's consistent, at least.

03:36:58.545 --> 03:36:59.225
DM: Patten.

03:37:00.145 --> 03:37:00.945
Kenzo: Was she, um...

03:37:03.525 --> 03:37:05.505
Delwath: Do you know anything about her relationship with her father?

03:37:08.405 --> 03:37:09.045
DM: Not really.

03:37:09.865 --> 03:37:10.205
DM: I mean,

03:37:12.245 --> 03:37:13.085
DM: all I know is

03:37:14.625 --> 03:37:19.505
DM: she's quite boastful and has told many, many dragonets that she is the daughter of Cha'mutte.

03:37:19.605 --> 03:37:20.545
Kenzo: Mm.

03:37:20.545 --> 03:37:23.725
DM: They've told me, the few who come up here every now and then.

03:37:23.725 --> 03:37:25.605
Delwath: Have they been here since, uh...

03:37:28.285 --> 03:37:29.805
Delwath: How long have the dragonets been here? Do you know?

03:37:30.345 --> 03:37:32.305
Unknown: Oh, you, you didn't know?

03:37:32.305 --> 03:37:37.225
DM: [coughs] You guys, like, don't really do your research, do you?

03:37:37.865 --> 03:37:39.205
Kenzo: We just got here. Come on. Cut us a break.

03:37:39.205 --> 03:37:40.325
Kenzo: Cut us a little... Give us a little break here.

03:37:40.525 --> 03:37:42.825
Delwath: I... They said forever, which is clearly not true.

03:37:43.125 --> 03:37:45.565
DM: Yeah. They're... We were, we were here...

03:37:46.585 --> 03:37:47.265
DM: My people

03:37:48.825 --> 03:37:50.845
DM: were on Hkar with the humans.

03:37:51.665 --> 03:37:51.945
Unknown: Oh.

03:37:52.065 --> 03:37:53.065
DM: We came across.

03:37:54.305 --> 03:37:56.965
Delwath: Didn't you just say you didn't realize there were so many of your people here?

03:37:57.725 --> 03:37:59.545
DM: I didn't know they survived the plague.

03:38:03.405 --> 03:38:11.345
DM: The story that I've fled, like many of us fled to the Feywild, to the Far East, all sorts of distant places when Drancor fell.

03:38:11.345 --> 03:38:13.325
DM: Well, even before Drancor fell.

03:38:14.885 --> 03:38:15.365
DM: A few,

03:38:16.885 --> 03:38:22.365
DM: you know, took in with the Polyron, and a few took in with Cha'mutte, but most of us just got out of dodge.

03:38:24.245 --> 03:38:24.365
Kenzo: Hm.

03:38:24.385 --> 03:38:26.705
DM: But we were there all the way from the beginning.

03:38:26.705 --> 03:38:28.685
DM: I just thought they were all slaughtered on this island.

03:38:32.205 --> 03:38:35.985
DM: If they say forever, I think they, like, mean it, probably since the island was made.

03:38:36.365 --> 03:38:36.985
Kenzo: Who made the island?

03:38:37.785 --> 03:38:39.345
DM: I don't know, like, wizards.

03:38:41.125 --> 03:38:42.125
Kenzo: Like human wizards?

03:38:42.125 --> 03:38:43.465
Wellby: Wizards don't, uh, don't do your research, huh?

03:38:44.685 --> 03:38:46.205
DM: Oh, well, do you have an answer for me?

03:38:47.045 --> 03:38:48.205
DM: Do you know who made the island?

03:38:48.625 --> 03:38:49.605
Wellby: Yes, but it's a secret.

03:38:49.605 --> 03:38:50.885
Kenzo: [laughs]

03:38:50.945 --> 03:38:52.225
DM: I don't like this one.

03:38:52.225 --> 03:38:55.145
Unknown: [coughs] Yeah, I don't know.

03:38:55.145 --> 03:38:57.685
DM: Like, there were all sorts of wizards back in the day.

03:38:58.145 --> 03:38:59.525
DM: They could do all kinds of things.

03:39:01.385 --> 03:39:02.745
DM: You didn't hear Rai's stories?

03:39:03.705 --> 03:39:05.205
DM: Oh, wait, how would you hear Rai's stories?

03:39:05.345 --> 03:39:06.965
Kenzo: Yeah. Never met the guy.

03:39:07.185 --> 03:39:08.145
Kenzo: Just had some weird rumors about him.

03:39:08.145 --> 03:39:09.785
DM: Yeah, he could probably have made this island.

03:39:10.765 --> 03:39:11.905
DM: Well, maybe not alone.

03:39:12.505 --> 03:39:14.145
Kenzo: He didn't... But he didn't make it, though.

03:39:14.185 --> 03:39:15.785
DM: No. It's way older than him.

03:39:16.025 --> 03:39:19.737
Kenzo: Yeah. Hm.

03:39:19.737 --> 03:39:20.077
Kenzo: Mm-hmm.

03:39:20.137 --> 03:39:23.597
DM: Yeah, they could do like, you know, Hkar, with like magic stuff.

03:39:23.657 --> 03:39:25.177
Kenzo: Is it, is it true that this island walked?

03:39:27.057 --> 03:39:27.757
DM: I, I think so.

03:39:28.597 --> 03:39:30.117
Seeker: Where did it come f- walk from?

03:39:30.877 --> 03:39:31.697
DM: Hkar.

03:39:31.697 --> 03:39:33.217
Unknown: Weren't you listening? [laughs]

03:39:33.257 --> 03:39:34.637
DM: Yeah. This guy gets it.

03:39:34.637 --> 03:39:35.897
Unknown: [laughs]

03:39:35.957 --> 03:39:37.957
DM: This one looks like an absent-minded professor.

03:39:37.957 --> 03:39:39.257
DM: I think that's what I'm gonna call him.

03:39:39.257 --> 03:39:39.877
Unknown: [laughs]

03:39:39.897 --> 03:39:41.237
DM: Dr. Absent-Minded.

03:39:41.357 --> 03:39:41.857
Unknown: Yes.

03:39:41.937 --> 03:39:42.997
Kenzo: Yeah, that's about right.

03:39:44.157 --> 03:39:44.377
Kenzo: Hmm.

03:39:46.837 --> 03:39:48.137
Kenzo: Uh, any idea who started the plague?

03:39:50.177 --> 03:39:50.677
Unknown: Shemuhitte?

03:39:50.677 --> 03:39:51.317
DM: Shemuhitte.

03:39:53.157 --> 03:39:53.317
Unknown: Right.

03:39:53.317 --> 03:39:54.397
DM: Are you not listening?

03:39:54.537 --> 03:39:55.157
Kenzo: Eh.

03:39:55.157 --> 03:39:58.437
Unknown: [laughs]

03:39:58.457 --> 03:39:59.377
DM: Eh-

03:39:59.397 --> 03:40:00.357
Kenzo: So the plague came here too?

03:40:03.097 --> 03:40:06.157
DM: I mean, Shemuhitte and Apollyon hated each other.

03:40:07.137 --> 03:40:07.237
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:40:10.797 --> 03:40:13.077
DM: His... Like he had some crappy tower.

03:40:13.197 --> 03:40:14.717
DM: Well, it probably wasn't that crappy actually.

03:40:14.717 --> 03:40:15.637
DM: It's kind of crappy now.

03:40:15.897 --> 03:40:16.417
Kenzo: Apollyon did?

03:40:16.437 --> 03:40:17.117
DM: I mean, nobody's been here.

03:40:17.117 --> 03:40:17.657
Unknown: Out in the west.

03:40:17.697 --> 03:40:18.977
DM: What, where you hide the forges?

03:40:19.037 --> 03:40:20.857
Unknown: Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah. That's where the forge is.

03:40:20.917 --> 03:40:21.297
Unknown: Yeah.

03:40:21.317 --> 03:40:21.337
DM: Yeah.

03:40:22.937 --> 03:40:30.697
Seeker: So is Shemuhitte's daughter's mission to d- protect the divine forge against Apollyon's return?

03:40:31.237 --> 03:40:31.597
DM: Maybe.

03:40:33.157 --> 03:40:34.537
DM: I know she doesn't like Apollyon.

03:40:34.717 --> 03:40:35.577
Unknown: Would she help us-

03:40:36.057 --> 03:40:37.837
Delwath: Yeah, see, I was going there earlier

03:40:37.837 --> 03:40:38.677
Unknown: ... to defeat him?

03:40:39.937 --> 03:40:40.677
Kenzo: Keep him imprisoned?

03:40:43.057 --> 03:40:43.577
DM: Maybe.

03:40:45.297 --> 03:40:45.497
Unknown: Like

03:40:46.697 --> 03:40:48.017
Unknown: there's an argument that we just-

03:40:48.077 --> 03:40:52.137
DM: If she genuinely thought you could kill Apollyon, she might be like, "Hey, go do it."

03:40:52.137 --> 03:40:58.657
Seeker: [sighs] Maybe we could even forge something

03:40:59.957 --> 03:41:00.597
Unknown: to help us.

03:41:01.077 --> 03:41:01.177
Kenzo: Hmm.

03:41:01.937 --> 03:41:03.237
Kenzo: If only we had an artificer.

03:41:03.237 --> 03:41:04.397
DM: [laughs]

03:41:04.437 --> 03:41:06.737
Wellby: Or to help us find the phylactery especially.

03:41:06.797 --> 03:41:06.957
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:41:09.737 --> 03:41:18.777
Delwath: I mean, there is the, we team up with Shemuhitte's daughter and an evil hobgoblin wizard to kill Apollyon and let the consequences be somebody else's problem.

03:41:18.777 --> 03:41:21.437
DM: Wait, the evil hobgoblin wizard is against Shemuhitte.

03:41:21.497 --> 03:41:23.137
Delwath: Oh, oh, oh, right. Never mind.

03:41:23.157 --> 03:41:23.777
Unknown: We gotta pick one.

03:41:23.777 --> 03:41:27.757
Kenzo: My enemy's friend is my friend's enemy's enemy.

03:41:28.137 --> 03:41:28.797
Unknown: Ah! [laughs]

03:41:28.797 --> 03:41:32.557
Delwath: We either team up with the evil hobgoblin wizard to kill Shemuhitte's daughter.

03:41:32.857 --> 03:41:33.077
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:41:33.477 --> 03:41:36.157
Delwath: Or we team... But she'd probably go join up with Apollyon.

03:41:37.617 --> 03:41:40.337
Delwath: Or we team up with Shemuhitte's daughter to kill Apollyon.

03:41:40.337 --> 03:41:41.057
Unknown: I like that one.

03:41:42.437 --> 03:41:43.997
Seeker: Well, could you get us an introduction?

03:41:45.237 --> 03:41:45.717
Unknown: No, I wouldn't-

03:41:45.737 --> 03:41:54.797
Delwath: Have you been listening? [laughs]

03:41:54.797 --> 03:41:58.157
Delwath: [laughs] But have you been over to the west where Apollyon's tower was?

03:42:01.217 --> 03:42:02.157
DM: I will be honest.

03:42:03.337 --> 03:42:04.357
Wellby: Is this a change?

03:42:04.357 --> 03:42:08.737
Unknown: [laughs]

03:42:08.737 --> 03:42:09.737
DM: That scares me.

03:42:10.377 --> 03:42:10.777
Kenzo: What? Why?

03:42:10.817 --> 03:42:10.977
Wellby: Hmm.

03:42:10.977 --> 03:42:17.417
Delwath: [coughs] So you've been there and it terrifies you, or you're just too scared to go?

03:42:17.577 --> 03:42:18.497
DM: Too scared to go.

03:42:18.577 --> 03:42:18.697
Wellby: Yeah.

03:42:18.757 --> 03:42:19.837
DM: You... Th- th-

03:42:19.857 --> 03:42:22.497
Delwath: Weren't you listening to the whole story of Apollyon and the fear?

03:42:22.577 --> 03:42:24.017
DM: Apollyon, like super evil.

03:42:24.197 --> 03:42:25.137
Kenzo: Yeah. Yeah, yeah. Oh, yeah.

03:42:25.257 --> 03:42:25.537
DM: Uh-

03:42:25.537 --> 03:42:26.557
Kenzo: He visits. I've seen him.

03:42:26.757 --> 03:42:26.977
DM: Yeah.

03:42:27.137 --> 03:42:28.057
Kenzo: I've made eye contact with the guy.

03:42:28.117 --> 03:42:28.397
Unknown: Okay. Okay.

03:42:28.417 --> 03:42:28.477
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:42:28.477 --> 03:42:30.437
DM: I have a, I have a, I have a task for you.

03:42:30.477 --> 03:42:31.337
Kenzo: Yeah. Hit me. Go ahead.

03:42:31.397 --> 03:42:41.397
DM: If you are a super e- evil wizard who had built a tower on top of a powerful divine forge, would you leave magical defenses or would you leave it completely undefended so anybody

03:42:41.397 --> 03:42:42.917
DM: could just walk in without doing...

03:42:43.477 --> 03:42:45.057
DM: without any care in the world?

03:42:45.137 --> 03:42:45.937
Kenzo: Magical defenses.

03:42:46.357 --> 03:42:47.117
Unknown: Bingo.

03:42:47.137 --> 03:42:47.157
Kenzo: Yes.

03:42:47.157 --> 03:42:48.197
Unknown: Why do you think I don't wanna go?

03:42:48.697 --> 03:42:49.437
Kenzo: Magical defenses.

03:42:49.697 --> 03:42:51.337
DM: Yes. You got it in one.

03:42:51.497 --> 03:42:52.117
Kenzo: Okay.

03:42:52.177 --> 03:42:53.477
Unknown: We- we're good at that though.

03:42:54.237 --> 03:42:54.477
Unknown: I mean,

03:42:56.097 --> 03:42:56.357
Unknown: yeah.

03:42:56.777 --> 03:42:57.397
Unknown: Or so we think.

03:42:58.857 --> 03:42:59.597
Unknown: We haven't been

03:43:01.157 --> 03:43:02.937
Seeker: completely annihilated as a group.

03:43:03.697 --> 03:43:04.657
Unknown: So maybe you should go there.

03:43:04.977 --> 03:43:06.677
Seeker: Yes. Tangling with those.

03:43:10.717 --> 03:43:11.437
Kenzo: Hmm. Hmm.

03:43:11.457 --> 03:43:18.417
Delwath: All right. What we should do is stay up for another hour to pick his brain about Drankor, meta write that down that we picked his brain about Drankor.

03:43:19.137 --> 03:43:19.177
DM: Yeah.

03:43:19.177 --> 03:43:22.017
Delwath: Take a long rest, and then either go to Apollyon's tower

03:43:23.597 --> 03:43:24.037
Unknown: or-

03:43:24.217 --> 03:43:25.897
Unknown: Yeah. To negotiate with the dragon

03:43:25.897 --> 03:43:28.577
Delwath: ... hatch a plan, which we need to decide what it would be.

03:43:29.577 --> 03:43:31.377
Delwath: But it's 2:20. I don't know if you wanted to take a break.

03:43:31.417 --> 03:43:32.977
Kenzo: Yeah. Yeah. I actually, I actually need to go do, do my call here.

03:43:33.017 --> 03:43:33.597
Unknown: Yeah, yeah. Let's take a break.

03:43:33.597 --> 03:43:34.257
Kenzo: It's the perfect, perfect time.

03:43:34.257 --> 03:43:34.877
Unknown: This is a good time to.

03:43:34.917 --> 03:43:35.057
Kenzo: Yeah.

03:43:35.057 --> 03:43:36.397
Unknown: So, I mean, let's...

03:43:37.697 --> 03:43:38.577
Unknown: That was really fun.

03:43:39.237 --> 03:43:39.477
Unknown: Let's see-

03:43:39.477 --> 03:43:42.257
Kenzo: Well, and I, I thought, yeah, w- we wanna hear some more ride stories too.

03:43:42.717 --> 03:43:46.117
DM: We can, we can do a little more Dimitar over the campfire.

03:43:46.377 --> 03:43:48.177
Kenzo: Yeah. Yeah. We can do that. We can do that like later.

03:43:48.177 --> 03:43:48.437
Unknown: A flashback.

03:43:48.437 --> 03:43:49.717
Kenzo: Like, like a flashback or like...

03:43:49.737 --> 03:43:49.737
Kenzo: Yeah, yeah.

03:43:49.737 --> 03:43:49.977
Unknown: We can do a flashback.

03:43:50.017 --> 03:43:59.677
Wellby: Yeah. So the choice when we c- reconvene is do we go to the dragon and start with negotiation of some kind to be figured out or do we go to Apollyon's tower and see what's going on there?

03:43:59.777 --> 03:43:59.957
Kenzo: So this is the thing-

03:44:00.217 --> 03:44:05.897
Delwath: Or do we just decide we should try and kill the dragon possibly by consulting with our hobgoblin wizard who's trapped?

03:44:06.277 --> 03:44:08.737
Kenzo: That's what we should do next. We should, we should consult with the hobgoblin.

03:44:08.737 --> 03:44:10.457
Kenzo: No matter what, we should talk to the hobgoblin wizard next.

03:44:10.477 --> 03:44:10.657
Unknown: That's true. Actually, that's true.

03:44:10.657 --> 03:44:12.197
Kenzo: Just to learn, just to get as much from her as we can.

03:44:12.337 --> 03:44:12.437
Unknown: Yeah.

03:44:12.437 --> 03:44:13.017
Kenzo: 'Cause this is the thing,

03:44:14.217 --> 03:44:15.057
Kenzo: the dragon,

03:44:16.837 --> 03:44:20.717
Kenzo: like we don't know yet the weird purpose that it is staying here for.

03:44:20.737 --> 03:44:20.857
Unknown: Right.

03:44:20.857 --> 03:44:25.137
Kenzo: Which is gonna be important and maybe potentially linked to whatever's going on in the west.

03:44:26.117 --> 03:44:26.217
Unknown: Right.

03:44:26.297 --> 03:44:36.437
Kenzo: So if we just go... So we need to s- we just need to understand a little bit more about the dynamics here 'cause there c- it could be that there's like a cool item or a thing that's in Apollyon's tower that the dragon can't get

03:44:36.437 --> 03:44:41.677
Kenzo: to, that if we got it, she would willing, be willing to trade with us or, you know...

